IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb4-common`
IMPORT `cb4-amendment`
IMPORT `cb4-amalgamation`
IMPORT `cb4-continuance`
IMPORT `cb4-borrowing-sale`
IMPORT `cb4-dissent`
IMPORT `cb4-reorg-arrangement`
IMPORT `cb4-going-private`
IMPORT `cb4-takeover`
IMPORT `cb4-dissolution`
IMPORT `cb4-court-liquidation`
IMPORT `cb4-liquidator`
IMPORT `cb4-after-dissolution`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Parts XV to XVIII -- THE SEAT LAYER (cb4).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice Canada consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; not verified against the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds shares in a corporation under the Canada Business
-- Corporations Act (an incorporator, a director or officer, or a shareholder, including a minority
-- shareholder), asking what the Act lets them do, what it requires of them, what they may require of the
-- corporation, and what can be done to them.
--
-- Every question takes plain inputs, one per fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as that
-- person would be asked; the records the layer-1 modules use are built inside each question, in its WHERE,
-- and the SAME module rule is called. No rule is restated here, and no layer-1 module changes to suit this
-- layer. Where the Act leaves a number or a judgment to the regulations, the articles or a court, the
-- question asks for it as a fact. Provisions that address only an official are asked for what they mean to
-- the person: what the person is owed, what may be done to them, by when.

§ `Canada Business Corporations Act -- the questions of a founder, director or shareholder (Parts XV to XVIII)`

§§ `Changing the articles (Part XV, ss 173 to 180)`

-- Articles are the corporation's founding document: its name, its classes of shares and their rights.
-- These questions are for a director or shareholder whose corporation is changing them.

-- ss 173(1), 176(6). Special resolution: two-thirds or more of the votes cast by the shareholders who
-- voted, or signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote. The class votes are in addition (fork F1).
@export Has my corporation validly adopted this change to its articles (ss 173(1), 176(6))?
GIVEN `the change` IS A `Kind of amendment under s 173(1)` @desc Which change to the articles is proposed? Choose the closest listed change, or "a change that s 173(1) does not list".
      `our stated capital is set out in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation's stated capital set out in its articles? (Matters only for a change to stated capital.)
      `the change in the number of directors complies with sections 107 and 112` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a change in the number of directors comply with sections 107 and 112? (Matters only for a change in the number of directors.)
      `the Act permits that provision to be in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this Act permit the provision to be set out in the articles? (Matters only for "any other provision".)
      `votes cast in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast in favour of the resolution by the shareholders who voted?
      `votes cast against` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast against it?
      `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on it?
      `every class or series with a separate vote approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If any class or series of shares had a separate vote on this change, did each one approve it by special resolution? Answer yes if none had a separate vote.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation validly adopted this change to its articles` IF
    `the amendment is adopted within s 173(1) and s 176(6)`
        (`the articles may be amended by special resolution within s 173(1)` `the change` `our stated capital is set out in the articles` `the change in the number of directors complies with sections 107 and 112` `the Act permits that provision to be in the articles` `the votes`)
        `every class or series with a separate vote approved`
    WHERE
        `the votes` MEANS `Vote tally` WITH
            `votes cast in favour` IS `votes cast in favour`
            `votes cast against` IS `votes cast against`
            `signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on the resolution` IS `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote`

-- ss 173(2), 174(5). "Acted on": the change has been carried out; after that the directors cannot revoke.
@export May the directors revoke the shareholders' special resolution without asking us again (ss 173(2), 174(5))?
GIVEN `the resolution authorized the directors to revoke it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the special resolution itself authorize the directors to revoke it?
      `the resolution has been acted on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the change the resolution approved already been carried out?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors revoke the shareholders' special resolution without asking us again` IF
    `the directors may revoke the resolution without further approval of the shareholders within s 173(2)` `the resolution authorized the directors to revoke it` `the resolution has been acted on`

-- s 173(3). A "number name" is a name that is only a designating number.
@export May the directors alone change our corporation's number name to a name in words (s 173(3))?
GIVEN `our corporation's name is a designating number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation's name a designating number?
      `the new name is a name in words` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the new name a name in words (a "verbal name")?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors alone change our corporation's number name to a name in words` IF
    `the directors may amend the articles to change a number name within s 173(3)` `our corporation's name is a designating number` `the new name is a name in words`

-- s 174(1), (2). A "constraint" limits who may be issued, may own or may transfer shares.
@export May my corporation put this constraint on who can hold its shares (ss 174(1), 174(2))?
GIVEN `our corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation a distributing corporation (one that has offered its securities to the public)?
      `issued shares remain outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do any of the corporation's issued shares remain outstanding?
      `those shares are held by more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the outstanding shares held by more than one person?
      `the constraint` IS A `Kind of constraint under s 174(1)` @desc Which constraint is proposed? Choose the closest listed one, or "a constraint that s 174(1) does not list".
      `the law concerned is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the law the constraint is meant to satisfy a law prescribed by the regulations? (Matters for the licence, publisher, financial-intermediary, qualifying and compliance constraints.)
      `the amendment follows the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amendment made in accordance with the regulations?
      `shares of the affected class or series are outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any shares of the class or series the constraint would affect outstanding?
      `those shares are already constrained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those shares already subject to a constraint of the "licences, permits, grants or benefits" kind?
      `votes cast in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast in favour of the resolution by the shareholders who voted?
      `votes cast against` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast against it?
      `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation put this constraint on who can hold its shares` IF
    `the corporation may amend its articles to constrain shares by special resolution within s 174(1)` `the proposal` `the votes`
    WHERE
        `the proposal` MEANS `Proposed constraint on shares (s 174)` WITH
            `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS `our corporation is a distributing corporation`
            `issued shares of the corporation remain outstanding` IS `issued shares remain outstanding`
            `those outstanding shares are held by more than one person` IS `those shares are held by more than one person`
            `the constraint proposed` IS `the constraint`
            `the law concerned is a prescribed law` IS `the law concerned is prescribed`
            `the amendment is made in accordance with the regulations` IS `the amendment follows the regulations`
            `shares of the class or series affected are outstanding` IS `shares of the affected class or series are outstanding`
            `those shares are already subject to a constraint permitted under paragraph 174(1)(c)` IS `those shares are already constrained`
        `the votes` MEANS `Vote tally` WITH
            `votes cast in favour` IS `votes cast in favour`
            `votes cast against` IS `votes cast against`
            `signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on the resolution` IS `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote`

-- s 174(3). "Level of Canadian ownership or control": a percentage the articles specify so that the
-- corporation or an affiliate keeps a licence, permit, grant or benefit.
@export May my corporation cap or bar a person's ownership of its shares (s 174(3))?
GIVEN `the cap or bar is made under the licences, permits, grants or benefits constraint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the cap or bar made under the constraint that protects a licence, permit, grant or benefit tied to Canadian ownership or control?
      `the person's ownership would adversely affect that level` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the person's ownership adversely affect the corporation's (or an affiliate's) ability to reach or keep the level of Canadian ownership or control?
      `that level is specified in the articles and meets the level the Act refers to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the level specified in the articles and equal to or above the specified level the constraint refers to?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation cap or bar a person's ownership of its shares` IF
    `the corporation may limit or prohibit a person's ownership of shares within s 174(3)` `the cap or bar is made under the licences, permits, grants or benefits constraint` `the person's ownership would adversely affect that level` `that level is specified in the articles and meets the level the Act refers to`

-- s 174(4).
@export May my corporation change or remove a constraint on its shares by special resolution (s 174(4))?
GIVEN `our corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation a distributing corporation?
      `issued shares remain outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do any of the corporation's issued shares remain outstanding?
      `those shares are held by more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the outstanding shares held by more than one person?
      `votes cast in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast in favour of the resolution by the shareholders who voted?
      `votes cast against` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast against it?
      `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation change or remove a constraint on its shares by special resolution` IF
    `the corporation may amend its articles to change or remove a constraint by special resolution within s 174(4)` `our corporation is a distributing corporation` `issued shares remain outstanding` `those shares are held by more than one person` `the votes`
    WHERE
        `the votes` MEANS `Vote tally` WITH
            `votes cast in favour` IS `votes cast in favour`
            `votes cast against` IS `votes cast against`
            `signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on the resolution` IS `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote`

-- s 174(7). The answer is "yes, valid" where the only defect is the failure; otherwise the Act does not say.
@export Is an issue or transfer of shares still valid although the corporation did not follow s 174 (s 174(7))?
GIVEN `the only defect is not following section 174 or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only defect that the corporation did not comply with section 174 or its regulations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an issue or transfer of shares still valid although the corporation did not follow s 174` IS
    `the issue, transfer or act is valid despite a failure to comply with s 174 within s 174(7)` `the only defect is not following section 174 or the regulations`

-- s 175(1). Section 137 says how a proposal is made.
@export May I make a proposal to amend the articles (s 175(1))?
GIVEN `I am a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the corporation?
      `I am a shareholder entitled to vote at an annual meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shareholder entitled to vote at an annual meeting of shareholders?
      `my proposal follows section 137` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proposal made in the way section 137 requires?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I make a proposal to amend the articles` IF
    `a person may make a proposal to amend the articles within s 175(1)` `I am a director` `I am a shareholder entitled to vote at an annual meeting` `my proposal follows section 137`

-- s 175(2).
@export Does the notice of the meeting say what the Act requires about a proposed amendment (s 175(2))?
GIVEN `the notice sets out the amendment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice of the meeting set out the proposed amendment?
      `shareholders have a right to dissent from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the proposed amendment give a dissenting shareholder the right under section 190 to be paid the fair value of their shares?
      `the notice states that right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the notice of the meeting say what the Act requires about a proposed amendment` IF
    `the notice of the meeting complies within s 175(2)` `the notice sets out the amendment` `shareholders have a right to dissent from it` `the notice states that right`

@export Is the amendment invalid because the notice did not state my right to dissent (s 175(2))?
GIVEN `leaving out the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was leaving out the statement of the right to dissent the only thing wrong with the notice?
GIVETH A `Effect on validity of leaving out the dissent statement`
DECIDE `Is the amendment invalid because the notice did not state my right to dissent` IS
    `the effect on the amendment of leaving out the dissent statement within s 175(2)` `leaving out the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice`

-- s 176(1) to (3). The "class vote": the holders of a class vote on their own on an amendment that
-- touches their class.
@export Am I entitled to vote separately, as a holder of a class of shares, on this proposed amendment (ss 176(1) to 176(3))?
GIVEN `what the amendment does to my class` IS AN `Effect of a proposed amendment on a class of shares (s 176(1))` @desc What does the amendment do to your class of shares? Choose the closest listed effect, or "no effect that s 176(1) lists".
      `the articles say my class has no separate vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles provide that the holders of your class may not vote separately? (Matters only for changes (a), (b) and (e).)
      `the new class is constrained and otherwise equal to mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the new class one whose issue, transfer or ownership is constrained under paragraph 174(1)(c) and which is otherwise equal to your class?
      `the amendment only adds a right to convert into such a class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the amendment only add a right to convert shares into an otherwise equal class that is constrained under paragraph 174(1)(c)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to vote separately, as a holder of a class of shares, on this proposed amendment` IF
    `the holders of the class are entitled to vote separately as a class within s 176(1)` `what the amendment does to my class` `the articles say my class has no separate vote` `the new class is constrained and otherwise equal to mine` `the amendment only adds a right to convert into such a class`

-- s 176(4). A "series" is a division of a class of shares.
@export Am I entitled to vote separately, as a holder of a series of shares, on this proposed amendment (s 176(4))?
GIVEN `my shares are a series of a class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold shares of a series of a class (a division of a class)?
      `my series is affected differently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the amendment affect your series differently from the other shares of the same class?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to vote separately, as a holder of a series of shares, on this proposed amendment` IF
    `the holders of a series are entitled to vote separately as a series within s 176(4)` `my shares are a series of a class` `my series is affected differently`

-- s 176(5).
@export Can I vote separately with my class or series although my shares carry no other vote (s 176(5))?
GIVEN `I am entitled to a separate vote under section 176(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 176(1) entitle the holders of your class or series to a separate vote on this amendment?
      `my shares otherwise carry the right to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your shares otherwise carry the right to vote?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I vote separately with my class or series although my shares carry no other vote` IF
    `the holders may vote separately even if the shares carry no other vote within s 176(5)` `I am entitled to a separate vote under section 176(1)` `my shares otherwise carry the right to vote`

-- s 176(6). This question is about ONE class or series: your own.
@export Has my class or series approved the amendment by special resolution (s 176(6))?
GIVEN `votes cast in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes did the holders of your class or series cast in favour?
      `votes cast against` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes did they cast against?
      `the resolution was signed by every holder of the class or series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution signed by all the holders of the class or series entitled to vote?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my class or series approved the amendment by special resolution` IF
    `every class or series entitled to vote separately has approved within s 176(6)` (LIST `my class's votes`)
    WHERE
        `my class's votes` MEANS `Vote tally` WITH
            `votes cast in favour` IS `votes cast in favour`
            `votes cast against` IS `votes cast against`
            `signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on the resolution` IS `the resolution was signed by every holder of the class or series`

-- ss 177(1), 177(2), 178.
@export Must my corporation now send articles of amendment to the Director (s 177(1))?
GIVEN `the amendment has been adopted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the amendment been adopted under section 173, 174 or 176?
      `the directors revoked the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors revoked the resolution under section 173(2) or 174(5)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my corporation now send articles of amendment to the Director` IF
    `the corporation must send articles of amendment to the Director within s 177(1)` `the amendment has been adopted` `the directors revoked the resolution`

@export Do the rules on reducing stated capital apply to this amendment (s 177(2))?
GIVEN `the amendment reduces stated capital or requires it to be reduced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the amendment reduce stated capital, or require it to be reduced?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the rules on reducing stated capital apply to this amendment` IF
    `subsections 38(3) and (4) apply to the amendment within s 177(2)` `the amendment reduces stated capital or requires it to be reduced`

@export Must the Director give my corporation a certificate of amendment (s 178)?
GIVEN `the Director has received our articles of amendment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director received your corporation's articles of amendment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director give my corporation a certificate of amendment` IF
    `the Director must issue a certificate of amendment within s 178` `the Director has received our articles of amendment`

-- s 179(1).
@export Has the amendment taken effect on the day I am asking about (s 179(1))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amendment` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of amendment? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-10)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking whether the amendment has taken effect? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-10)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the amendment taken effect on the day I am asking about` IF
    `the amendment is effective and the articles stand amended on a day within s 179(1)` `the date shown in the certificate of amendment` `the day I am asking about`

-- s 179(2).
@export Does the amendment of the articles affect a claim, liability or proceeding that already exists (s 179(2))?
GIVEN `the matter is an existing claim, liability or proceeding involving the corporation or its directors or officers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter an existing cause of action, claim, liability to prosecution, or a civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding to which the corporation or its directors or officers is a party?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the amendment of the articles affect a claim, liability or proceeding that already exists` IS
    `whether a matter is unaffected by an amendment within s 179(2)` `the matter is an existing claim, liability or proceeding involving the corporation or its directors or officers`

-- s 180.
@export Must the directors restate our articles (s 180(1))?
GIVEN `the Director has reasonably directed the directors to restate the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director reasonably directed the directors to restate the articles?
GIVETH A `Directors' position on restating the articles`
DECIDE `Must the directors restate our articles` IS
    `the directors' position on restating the articles within s 180(1)` `the Director has reasonably directed the directors to restate the articles`

@export Must we send the restated articles to the Director (s 180(2))?
GIVEN `the articles have been restated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the articles of incorporation been restated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must we send the restated articles to the Director` IF
    `the restated articles must be sent to the Director within s 180(2)` `the articles have been restated`

@export Must the Director give us a restated certificate of incorporation (s 180(3))?
GIVEN `the Director has received our restated articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director received your restated articles of incorporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director give us a restated certificate of incorporation` IF
    `the Director must issue a restated certificate of incorporation within s 180(3)` `the Director has received our restated articles`

@export Do the restated articles replace our earlier articles on the day I am asking about (s 180(4))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the restated certificate` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the restated certificate of incorporation? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-04-01)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-04-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the restated articles replace our earlier articles on the day I am asking about` IF
    `the restated articles are effective and supersede the earlier articles on a day within s 180(4)` `the date shown in the restated certificate` `the day I am asking about`

§§ `Amalgamating with another corporation (Part XV, ss 181 to 186.1)`

-- To "amalgamate" is to join two or more corporations into one. These questions are for a director or
-- shareholder of a corporation that is amalgamating.

-- s 181.
@export Can my corporation amalgamate with other corporations (s 181)?
GIVEN `the number of corporations that propose to amalgamate` IS A NUMBER @desc How many corporations propose to amalgamate, counting yours?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my corporation amalgamate with other corporations` IF
    `the corporations may amalgamate and continue as one corporation within s 181` `the number of corporations that propose to amalgamate`

-- s 182(1).
@export Does our amalgamation agreement contain everything the Act requires (s 182(1))?
GIVEN `every corporation proposing to amalgamate has signed the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has every corporation proposing to amalgamate entered into the agreement?
      `it sets out the provisions that section 6 requires in articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement set out the provisions that section 6 requires in articles of incorporation?
      `it names and gives the address of each proposed director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out the name and address of each proposed director of the amalgamated corporation?
      `it sets out how shares are converted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out how the shares of each amalgamating corporation are converted into shares or other securities of the amalgamated corporation?
      `some shares are not converted into securities of the amalgamated corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are some shares of an amalgamating corporation not to be converted into securities of the amalgamated corporation?
      `it sets out what those holders receive instead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does it set out the money or securities those holders receive in addition to or instead?
      `it sets out how fractional shares are paid for in money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out how money is paid instead of fractional shares?
      `it states whether the by-laws are those of an amalgamating corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state whether the by-laws of the amalgamated corporation are to be those of one of the amalgamating corporations?
      `the by-laws are not those of an amalgamating corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the by-laws NOT to be those of one of the amalgamating corporations?
      `it includes a copy of the proposed by-laws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include a copy of the proposed by-laws?
      `it sets out the arrangements to perfect the amalgamation and manage the new corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out the details of the arrangements needed to perfect the amalgamation and to manage and operate the amalgamated corporation afterwards?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our amalgamation agreement contain everything the Act requires` IF
    `the amalgamation agreement contains what s 182(1) requires` `our agreement`
    WHERE
        `our agreement` MEANS `Amalgamation agreement (s 182)` WITH
            `every corporation proposing to amalgamate has entered into the agreement` IS `every corporation proposing to amalgamate has signed the agreement`
            `sets out the provisions required to be in articles of incorporation under section 6` IS `it sets out the provisions that section 6 requires in articles`
            `sets out the name and address of each proposed director of the amalgamated corporation` IS `it names and gives the address of each proposed director`
            `sets out how the shares of each amalgamating corporation are to be converted into shares or other securities of the amalgamated corporation` IS `it sets out how shares are converted`
            `some shares of an amalgamating corporation are not to be converted into securities of the amalgamated corporation` IS `some shares are not converted into securities of the amalgamated corporation`
            `sets out the money or securities those holders are to receive in addition to or instead of securities of the amalgamated corporation` IS `it sets out what those holders receive instead`
            `sets out how money is to be paid instead of fractional shares` IS `it sets out how fractional shares are paid for in money`
            `states whether the by-laws are to be those of one of the amalgamating corporations` IS `it states whether the by-laws are those of an amalgamating corporation`
            `the by-laws are not to be those of one of the amalgamating corporations` IS `the by-laws are not those of an amalgamating corporation`
            `includes a copy of the proposed by-laws` IS `it includes a copy of the proposed by-laws`
            `sets out details of arrangements necessary to perfect the amalgamation and provide for the subsequent management and operation` IS `it sets out the arrangements to perfect the amalgamation and manage the new corporation`

-- s 182(2).
@export Does our agreement deal properly with shares one amalgamating corporation holds in another (s 182(2))?
GIVEN `one amalgamating corporation holds shares of another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are shares of one amalgamating corporation held by or on behalf of another amalgamating corporation?
      `the agreement cancels those shares without repaying capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement provide for cancelling those shares without any repayment of capital?
      `the agreement converts those shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement make provision for converting those shares into shares of the amalgamated corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our agreement deal properly with shares one amalgamating corporation holds in another` IF
    `the agreement deals as s 182(2) requires with shares held within the group` `one amalgamating corporation holds shares of another` `the agreement cancels those shares without repaying capital` `the agreement converts those shares`

-- s 183(1).
@export Must the directors put the amalgamation agreement to the shareholders at a meeting (s 183(1))?
GIVEN `it is an amalgamation under the agreement of section 182 and not a short-form one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amalgamation made under an agreement (section 182), and not a short-form amalgamation under section 184?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the directors put the amalgamation agreement to the shareholders at a meeting` IF
    `the directors of each amalgamating corporation must submit the agreement to a meeting of shareholders within s 183(1)` `it is an amalgamation under the agreement of section 182 and not a short-form one`

-- s 183(2). Section 135 says how a notice of a meeting is given.
@export Does the notice of the amalgamation meeting say what the Act requires (s 183(2))?
GIVEN `the notice complies with section 135` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice comply with section 135 (notice of a meeting of shareholders)?
      `the notice goes to every shareholder of every amalgamating corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice sent to each shareholder of each amalgamating corporation?
      `a copy or summary of the agreement is with the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice include, or come with, a copy or summary of the amalgamation agreement?
      `shareholders have the right to dissent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a dissenting shareholder entitled under section 190 to be paid the fair value of their shares for this amalgamation?
      `the notice states that right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the notice of the amalgamation meeting say what the Act requires` IF
    `the notice of the meeting complies within s 183(2)` `the notice complies with section 135` `the notice goes to every shareholder of every amalgamating corporation` `a copy or summary of the agreement is with the notice` `shareholders have the right to dissent` `the notice states that right`

@export Is the amalgamation invalid because the notice did not state my right to dissent (s 183(2)(b))?
GIVEN `leaving out the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was leaving out the statement of the right to dissent the only thing wrong with the notice?
GIVETH A `Effect on validity of leaving out the dissent statement`
DECIDE `Is the amalgamation invalid because the notice did not state my right to dissent` IS
    `the effect on the amalgamation of leaving out the dissent statement within s 183(2)(b)` `leaving out the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice`

-- s 183(3).
@export Can I vote on the amalgamation although my shares carry no other vote (s 183(3))?
GIVEN `my shares otherwise carry the right to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your shares otherwise carry the right to vote?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I vote on the amalgamation although my shares carry no other vote` IF
    `the share carries the right to vote on the amalgamation agreement within s 183(3)` `my shares otherwise carry the right to vote`

-- s 183(4). The test is the one s 176 sets for an amendment of the articles.
@export Am I entitled to vote separately, with my class or series, on the amalgamation agreement (s 183(4))?
GIVEN `what the agreement does to my class` IS AN `Effect of a proposed amendment on a class of shares (s 176(1))` @desc What would a provision of the agreement do to your class if it were in an amendment of the articles? Choose the closest listed effect, or "no effect that s 176(1) lists".
      `the articles say my class has no separate vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles provide that the holders of your class may not vote separately? (Matters only for some effects.)
      `the new class is constrained and otherwise equal to mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the new class one whose issue, transfer or ownership is constrained under paragraph 174(1)(c) and which is otherwise equal to your class?
      `the agreement only adds a right to convert into such a class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement only add a right to convert shares into an otherwise equal class that is constrained under paragraph 174(1)(c)?
      `my shares are a series of a class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold shares of a series of a class?
      `my series is affected differently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your series affected differently from the other shares of the same class?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to vote separately, with my class or series, on the amalgamation agreement` IF
    `the holders of a class or series are entitled to vote separately on the amalgamation agreement within s 183(4)` `what the agreement does to my class` `the articles say my class has no separate vote` `the new class is constrained and otherwise equal to mine` `the agreement only adds a right to convert into such a class` `my shares are a series of a class` `my series is affected differently`

-- s 183(5).
@export Have my corporation's shareholders approved the amalgamation agreement (s 183(5))?
GIVEN `votes cast in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast in favour of the agreement by the shareholders of your corporation who voted?
      `votes cast against` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast against it?
      `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on it?
      `every class or series with a separate vote approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If any class or series of your corporation had a separate vote, did each one approve by special resolution? Answer yes if none had a separate vote.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have my corporation's shareholders approved the amalgamation agreement` IF
    `the shareholders of an amalgamating corporation have approved the agreement within s 183(5)` `our votes` `every class or series with a separate vote approved`
    WHERE
        `our votes` MEANS `Vote tally` WITH
            `votes cast in favour` IS `votes cast in favour`
            `votes cast against` IS `votes cast against`
            `signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on the resolution` IS `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote`

@export Is the amalgamation agreement adopted by all the amalgamating corporations (s 183(5))?
GIVEN `my corporation's shareholders have approved it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the shareholders of your corporation approved the agreement by special resolution (and each class with a separate vote)?
      `the shareholders of every other amalgamating corporation have approved it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the shareholders of every other amalgamating corporation approved it in the same way?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the amalgamation agreement adopted by all the amalgamating corporations` IF
    `the amalgamation agreement is adopted within s 183(5)` (LIST `my corporation's shareholders have approved it`, `the shareholders of every other amalgamating corporation have approved it`)

-- s 183(6).
@export May the directors terminate the amalgamation agreement even though the shareholders approved it (s 183(6))?
GIVEN `the agreement says the directors may terminate it before the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement provide that the directors of an amalgamating corporation may terminate it before a certificate of amalgamation is issued?
      `a certificate of amalgamation has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a certificate of amalgamation been issued?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors terminate the amalgamation agreement even though the shareholders approved it` IF
    `the directors may terminate the agreement notwithstanding the shareholders' approval within s 183(6)` `the agreement says the directors may terminate it before the certificate` `a certificate of amalgamation has been issued`

-- s 184(1). "Vertical": a parent and its subsidiaries.
@export Can a holding corporation and its subsidiaries amalgamate by directors' resolutions alone (s 184(1))?
GIVEN `we are a holding corporation and one or more of its subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the amalgamating corporations a holding corporation and one or more of its subsidiary corporations?
      `each corporation's directors approved by resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors of each amalgamating corporation approve the amalgamation by resolution?
      `each subsidiary's issued shares are all held within the group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the issued shares of each amalgamating subsidiary held by one or more of the other amalgamating corporations?
      `the resolutions cancel the subsidiaries' shares without repaying capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the resolutions provide that the shares of each amalgamating subsidiary are cancelled without any repayment of capital?
      `the resolutions keep the holding corporation's articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the resolutions provide that the articles of amalgamation are the same as the holding corporation's, except as prescribed?
      `the resolutions issue no securities and keep the holding corporation's stated capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the resolutions provide that no securities are issued and the stated capital is the same as the holding corporation's?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a holding corporation and its subsidiaries amalgamate by directors' resolutions alone` IF
    `the corporations may amalgamate without complying with sections 182 and 183 within s 184(1)` `we are a holding corporation and one or more of its subsidiaries` `each corporation's directors approved by resolution` `each subsidiary's issued shares are all held within the group` `the resolutions cancel the subsidiaries' shares without repaying capital` `the resolutions keep the holding corporation's articles` `the resolutions issue no securities and keep the holding corporation's stated capital`

-- s 184(2). "Horizontal": sister subsidiaries of one holding body corporate.
@export Can wholly-owned subsidiaries of one holding company amalgamate by directors' resolutions alone (s 184(2))?
GIVEN `we are wholly-owned subsidiaries of the same holding body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the amalgamating corporations two or more wholly-owned subsidiaries of the same holding body corporate?
      `each corporation's directors approved by resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors of each amalgamating corporation approve the amalgamation by resolution?
      `the resolutions cancel all but one subsidiary's shares without repaying capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the resolutions provide that the shares of all but one of the subsidiaries are cancelled without any repayment of capital?
      `the resolutions keep the articles of the subsidiary not cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the resolutions provide that the articles of amalgamation are the same as those of the subsidiary whose shares are not cancelled, except as prescribed?
      `the resolutions add the cancelled subsidiaries' stated capital to the other's` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the resolutions provide that the stated capital of the subsidiaries whose shares are cancelled is added to that of the subsidiary whose shares are not cancelled?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can wholly-owned subsidiaries of one holding company amalgamate by directors' resolutions alone` IF
    `the subsidiary corporations may amalgamate without complying with sections 182 and 183 within s 184(2)` `we are wholly-owned subsidiaries of the same holding body corporate` `each corporation's directors approved by resolution` `the resolutions cancel all but one subsidiary's shares without repaying capital` `the resolutions keep the articles of the subsidiary not cancelled` `the resolutions add the cancelled subsidiaries' stated capital to the other's`

-- s 185(1).
@export Must my corporation now send articles of amalgamation to the Director (s 185(1))?
GIVEN `the amalgamation was adopted under section 183` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the amalgamation been adopted under section 183?
      `the amalgamation was approved under section 184` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the amalgamation been approved under section 184 (short form)?
      `the directors terminated the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors terminate the agreement under section 183(6)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my corporation now send articles of amalgamation to the Director` IF
    `the corporation must send articles of amalgamation to the Director within s 185(1)` `the amalgamation was adopted under section 183` `the amalgamation was approved under section 184` `the directors terminated the agreement`

@export Have we sent the articles of amalgamation to the Director as the Act requires (s 185(1))?
GIVEN `the articles are in the form the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the articles of amalgamation in the form the Director fixes?
      `the documents under sections 19 and 106 went with them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the documents required by sections 19 and 106 sent with them?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have we sent the articles of amalgamation to the Director as the Act requires` IF
    `the articles of amalgamation have been sent as s 185(1) requires` `the articles are in the form the Director fixes` `the documents under sections 19 and 106 went with them`

-- s 185(2). A "statutory declaration" is a sworn statement made before an authorized person.
@export Does the statutory declaration attached to our articles of amalgamation meet the Act (s 185(2))?
GIVEN `a director or an officer of each amalgamating corporation made a statutory declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a statutory declaration of a director or an officer of each amalgamating corporation attached to the articles?
      `we can pay our liabilities as they fall due` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds for believing that each amalgamating corporation is, and the amalgamated corporation will be, able to pay its liabilities as they become due?
      `the assets will be worth at least the liabilities and stated capital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds for believing that the realizable value of the amalgamated corporation's assets will not be less than its liabilities plus the stated capital of all classes?
      `no creditor will be prejudiced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds for believing that no creditor will be prejudiced by the amalgamation?
      `adequate notice has been given to known creditors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds for believing that adequate notice has been given to all known creditors of the amalgamating corporations?
      `no creditor objects on grounds that are not frivolous or vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds for believing that no creditor objects otherwise than on frivolous or vexatious grounds?
      `the Director is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Director satisfied that the declaration establishes those grounds?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the statutory declaration attached to our articles of amalgamation meet the Act` IF
    `the statutory declaration meets s 185(2)` `a director or an officer of each amalgamating corporation made a statutory declaration` `we can pay our liabilities as they fall due` `the assets will be worth at least the liabilities and stated capital` `no creditor will be prejudiced` `adequate notice has been given to known creditors` `no creditor objects on grounds that are not frivolous or vexatious` `the Director is satisfied`

-- s 185(3)(a). The claim must exceed one thousand dollars.
@export Must we send a written notice of the amalgamation to this creditor (s 185(3)(a))?
GIVEN `the creditor's claim against us in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the creditor's claim against the corporation, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must we send a written notice of the amalgamation to this creditor` IF
    `the creditor must be sent a written notice within s 185(3)(a)` `the creditor's claim against us in dollars`

-- s 185(3).
@export Have we given our creditors adequate notice of the amalgamation (s 185(3))?
GIVEN `we sent a written notice to every known creditor with a claim over $1,000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a written notice sent to each known creditor having a claim against the corporation of more than one thousand dollars?
      `we published a notice once in a newspaper at the registered office's place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a notice published once in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office?
      `we gave reasonable notice in each province where we carry on business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was reasonable notice given in each province where the corporation carries on business?
      `each notice says we intend to amalgamate with the named corporations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does each notice state that the corporation intends to amalgamate with one or more specified corporations in accordance with this Act?
      `each notice says a creditor may object within thirty days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does each notice state that a creditor may object within thirty days from the date of the notice?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have we given our creditors adequate notice of the amalgamation` IF
    `adequate notice has been given to creditors within s 185(3)` `we sent a written notice to every known creditor with a claim over $1,000` `we published a notice once in a newspaper at the registered office's place` `we gave reasonable notice in each province where we carry on business` `each notice says we intend to amalgamate with the named corporations` `each notice says a creditor may object within thirty days`

@export What is the last day on which a creditor may object to the amalgamation (s 185(3)(c))?
GIVEN `the date of our notice to creditors` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the notice to creditors? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-01-31)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day on which a creditor may object to the amalgamation` IS
    `the last day on which a creditor may object within s 185(3)(c)` `the date of our notice to creditors`

-- s 185(4).
@export Must the Director give us a certificate of amalgamation (s 185(4))?
GIVEN `the Director has received our articles of amalgamation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director received the articles of amalgamation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director give us a certificate of amalgamation` IF
    `the Director must issue a certificate of amalgamation within s 185(4)` `the Director has received our articles of amalgamation`

-- s 186. The date shown in the certificate of amalgamation is the day the effects begin.
@export Has the amalgamation taken effect on the day I am asking about (s 186(a))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of amalgamation? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-05-01)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-05-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the amalgamation taken effect on the day I am asking about` IF
    `the amalgamation and continuance as one corporation are effective on a day within s 186(a)` `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the day I am asking about`

@export Does the property of each amalgamating corporation now belong to the amalgamated corporation (s 186(b))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of amalgamation? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-05-01)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-05-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the property of each amalgamating corporation now belong to the amalgamated corporation` IF
    `the property of each amalgamating corporation is the amalgamated corporation's on a day within s 186(b)` `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the day I am asking about`

@export Is the amalgamated corporation liable for the obligations of the corporation I dealt with (s 186(c))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of amalgamation? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-05-01)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-05-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the amalgamated corporation liable for the obligations of the corporation I dealt with` IF
    `the amalgamated corporation is liable for the obligations of each amalgamating corporation on a day within s 186(c)` `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the day I am asking about`

@export Is my existing claim or liability unaffected by the amalgamation (s 186(d))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of amalgamation? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-05-01)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-05-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my existing claim or liability unaffected by the amalgamation` IF
    `an existing cause of action, claim or liability to prosecution is unaffected on a day within s 186(d)` `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the day I am asking about`

@export Can a proceeding against the corporation I dealt with be continued against the amalgamated corporation (s 186(e))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of amalgamation? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-05-01)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-05-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a proceeding against the corporation I dealt with be continued against the amalgamated corporation` IF
    `a pending proceeding by or against an amalgamating corporation may be continued by or against the amalgamated corporation on a day within s 186(e)` `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the day I am asking about`

@export Can a judgment I hold against an amalgamating corporation be enforced against the amalgamated corporation (s 186(f))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of amalgamation? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-05-01)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-05-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a judgment I hold against an amalgamating corporation be enforced against the amalgamated corporation` IF
    `a conviction, ruling, order or judgment may be enforced by or against the amalgamated corporation on a day within s 186(f)` `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the day I am asking about`

@export Are the articles of amalgamation now treated as the amalgamated corporation's articles of incorporation (s 186(g))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of amalgamation? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-05-01)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-05-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the articles of amalgamation now treated as the amalgamated corporation's articles of incorporation` IF
    `the articles and the certificate of amalgamation are deemed the articles and certificate of incorporation on a day within s 186(g)` `the date shown in the certificate of amalgamation` `the day I am asking about`

-- s 186.1. The other Acts: Bank Act, Canada Cooperatives Act, Cooperative Credit Associations Act,
-- Insurance Companies Act, Trust and Loan Companies Act.
@export May my corporation amalgamate under one of the other federal Acts (s 186.1(1))?
GIVEN `the amalgamation is under one of those other Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amalgamation with bodies corporate under the Bank Act, the Canada Cooperatives Act, the Cooperative Credit Associations Act, the Insurance Companies Act or the Trust and Loan Companies Act?
      `the shareholders first authorized it in accordance with section 183` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the shareholders first authorize it in accordance with section 183?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation amalgamate under one of the other federal Acts` IS
    `the corporation may amalgamate pursuant to another federal Act within s 186.1(1)` `the amalgamation is under one of those other Acts` `the shareholders first authorized it in accordance with section 183`

@export May my corporation make a short-form amalgamation under one of the other federal Acts (s 186.1(2))?
GIVEN `the amalgamation is a short-form one under one of those other Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amalgamation a short-form amalgamation under one of the other federal Acts named in section 186.1(1)?
      `the directors first authorized it in accordance with section 184` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors first authorize it in accordance with section 184?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation make a short-form amalgamation under one of the other federal Acts` IS
    `the corporation may amalgamate in short form pursuant to another federal Act within s 186.1(2)` `the amalgamation is a short-form one under one of those other Acts` `the directors first authorized it in accordance with section 184`

@export Must the Director file our notice and give us a certificate of discontinuance (s 186.1(3))?
GIVEN `the Director has received our notice that we have amalgamated under another federal Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director received a notice that the corporation has amalgamated under one of those other Acts?
      `the notice is satisfactory to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice satisfactory to the Director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director file our notice and give us a certificate of discontinuance` IF
    `the Director must file the notice and issue a certificate of discontinuance within s 186.1(3)` `the Director has received our notice that we have amalgamated under another federal Act` `the notice is satisfactory to the Director`

@export Is our notice treated as articles in the form the Director fixes (s 186.1(4))?
GIVEN `the document is the notice of an amalgamation under another federal Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document the notice, referred to in section 186.1(3), that the corporation has amalgamated under one of the other federal Acts?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our notice treated as articles in the form the Director fixes` IF
    `the notice is deemed to be articles in the form the Director fixes for section 262 within s 186.1(4)` `the document is the notice of an amalgamation under another federal Act`

@export Does the Canada Business Corporations Act still apply to my corporation on the day I am asking about (s 186.1(5))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of discontinuance` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of discontinuance? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-01)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Canada Business Corporations Act still apply to my corporation on the day I am asking about` IF
    `this Act still applies to the corporation on a day within s 186.1(5)` `the date shown in the certificate of discontinuance` `the day I am asking about`

@export Is my corporation freed from the articles-of-amalgamation duty of section 185 when we amalgamate under another federal Act (s 186.1(6))?
GIVEN `we amalgamate under one of those other Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation amalgamate under one of the other federal Acts named in section 186.1(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation freed from the articles-of-amalgamation duty of section 185 when we amalgamate under another federal Act` IF
    `section 185 does not apply to the corporation within s 186.1(6)` `we amalgamate under one of those other Acts`

§§ `Moving a corporation in or out: continuance (Part XV, ss 187 and 188)`

-- "Continuance" moves a corporation from one statute to another without winding it up. Section 187 is for
-- a body corporate coming IN to the Canada Business Corporations Act; section 188 is for a corporation
-- going OUT of it.

-- s 187(1).
@export May our body corporate apply to be continued under the Canada Business Corporations Act (s 187(1))?
GIVEN `we were incorporated otherwise than by or under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your body corporate incorporated otherwise than by or under an Act of Parliament (for example, under a provincial Act or foreign law)?
      `our home law authorizes us to apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the laws of the jurisdiction where you are incorporated authorize you to apply for continuance elsewhere?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our body corporate apply to be continued under the Canada Business Corporations Act` IF
    `the body corporate may apply to the Director for a certificate of continuance within s 187(1)` `we were incorporated otherwise than by or under an Act of Parliament` `our home law authorizes us to apply`

-- s 187(2).
@export Can our articles of continuance make an amendment without stating it (s 187(2))?
GIVEN `we are applying for continuance under section 187(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your body corporate applying for continuance under section 187(1)?
      `a corporation under this Act may make that amendment to its articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amendment one that a corporation incorporated under this Act may make to its articles?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can our articles of continuance make an amendment without stating it` IF
    `the articles of continuance may effect the amendment without stating it within s 187(2)` `we are applying for continuance under section 187(1)` `a corporation under this Act may make that amendment to its articles`

-- s 187(3).
@export Have we sent our articles of continuance to the Director as the Act requires (s 187(3))?
GIVEN `the articles are in the form the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the articles of continuance in the form the Director fixes?
      `the documents under sections 19 and 106 went with them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the documents required by sections 19 and 106 sent with them?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have we sent our articles of continuance to the Director as the Act requires` IF
    `the articles of continuance have been sent as s 187(3) requires` `the articles are in the form the Director fixes` `the documents under sections 19 and 106 went with them`

-- s 187(4).
@export Must the Director give us a certificate of continuance (s 187(4))?
GIVEN `the Director has received our articles of continuance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director received your articles of continuance?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director give us a certificate of continuance` IF
    `the Director must issue a certificate of continuance within s 187(4)` `the Director has received our articles of continuance`

-- s 187(5). The date shown in the certificate of continuance is the day the effects begin.
@export Are we a corporation under the Canada Business Corporations Act on the day I am asking about (s 187(5)(a))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of continuance` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of continuance? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-15)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-15)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are we a corporation under the Canada Business Corporations Act on the day I am asking about` IF
    `the body corporate is a corporation to which this Act applies on a day within s 187(5)(a)` `the date shown in the certificate of continuance` `the day I am asking about`

@export Are our articles of continuance now our articles of incorporation (s 187(5)(b))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of continuance` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of continuance? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-15)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-15)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are our articles of continuance now our articles of incorporation` IF
    `the articles of continuance are deemed the articles of incorporation on a day within s 187(5)(b)` `the date shown in the certificate of continuance` `the day I am asking about`

@export Is our certificate of continuance now our certificate of incorporation (s 187(5)(c))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of continuance` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of continuance? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-15)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-15)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our certificate of continuance now our certificate of incorporation` IF
    `the certificate of continuance is deemed the certificate of incorporation on a day within s 187(5)(c)` `the date shown in the certificate of continuance` `the day I am asking about`

-- s 187(6).
@export Will the Director tell the authorities of our home jurisdiction about our continuance (s 187(6))?
GIVEN `the Director has issued our certificate of continuance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director issued your certificate of continuance?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the Director tell the authorities of our home jurisdiction about our continuance` IF
    `the Director must send a copy of the certificate to the official or body of the home jurisdiction within s 187(6)` `the Director has issued our certificate of continuance`

-- s 187(7). Each answer is yes once the body corporate has been continued as a corporation under this Act.
@export After continuance, does our property stay ours (s 187(7)(a))?
GIVEN `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your body corporate been continued as a corporation under this Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `After continuance, does our property stay ours` IF
    `the property of the body corporate continues to be the corporation's within s 187(7)(a)` `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act`

@export After continuance, are we still liable for the obligations we had before (s 187(7)(b))?
GIVEN `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your body corporate been continued as a corporation under this Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `After continuance, are we still liable for the obligations we had before` IF
    `the corporation continues to be liable for the body corporate's obligations within s 187(7)(b)` `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act`

@export After continuance, is an existing claim or liability to prosecution unaffected (s 187(7)(c))?
GIVEN `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your body corporate been continued as a corporation under this Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `After continuance, is an existing claim or liability to prosecution unaffected` IF
    `an existing cause of action, claim or liability to prosecution is unaffected by the continuance within s 187(7)(c)` `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act`

@export After continuance, can a pending proceeding be carried on by or against the corporation (s 187(7)(d))?
GIVEN `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your body corporate been continued as a corporation under this Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `After continuance, can a pending proceeding be carried on by or against the corporation` IF
    `a pending proceeding by or against the body corporate may be continued by or against the corporation within s 187(7)(d)` `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act`

@export After continuance, can a judgment or order be enforced by or against the corporation (s 187(7)(e))?
GIVEN `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your body corporate been continued as a corporation under this Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `After continuance, can a judgment or order be enforced by or against the corporation` IF
    `a conviction, ruling, order or judgment may be enforced by or against the corporation within s 187(7)(e)` `we have been continued as a corporation under this Act`

-- s 187(8).
@export Is my share, issued before our continuance, treated as validly issued under this Act (s 187(8))?
GIVEN `my share was issued before our body corporate was continued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your share issued before your body corporate was continued under this Act?
      `section 49(8) applies to my share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 49(8) apply to your share?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my share, issued before our continuance, treated as validly issued under this Act` IS
    `the share is deemed to have been issued in compliance with this Act within s 187(8)` `my share was issued before our body corporate was continued under this Act` `section 49(8) applies to my share`

@export Do I keep my rights, and my liabilities, in respect of my share after our continuance (s 187(8))?
GIVEN `my share was issued before our body corporate was continued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your share issued before your body corporate was continued under this Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I keep my rights, and my liabilities, in respect of my share after our continuance` IS
    `the holder keeps the rights and the liabilities in respect of the share within s 187(8)` `my share was issued before our body corporate was continued under this Act`

-- s 187(9).
@export May we issue a bearer share certificate when a holder converts a registered one (s 187(9))?
GIVEN `the certificate was issued in registered form before continuance and is convertible to bearer form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate issued in registered form before the continuance, and is it convertible to bearer form?
      `the holder exercises the conversion privilege` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the holder exercise the conversion privilege attached to the certificate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May we issue a bearer share certificate when a holder converts a registered one` IF
    `the corporation may issue a share certificate in bearer form within s 187(9)` `the certificate was issued in registered form before continuance and is convertible to bearer form` `the holder exercises the conversion privilege`

-- s 187(10).
@export Does my instrument count as a "share" for the continuance rules about issued shares and bearer certificates (s 187(10))?
GIVEN `the kind of instrument` IS A `Kind of instrument for s 187(10)` @desc Which kind of instrument is it? Choose the closest listed kind, or "an instrument that is none of these".
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my instrument count as a "share" for the continuance rules about issued shares and bearer certificates` IF
    `the instrument is a share for subsections 187(8) and 187(9) within s 187(10)` `the kind of instrument`

-- s 187(11), (12).
@export May the Director let us go on calling our shares par value shares (s 187(11))?
GIVEN `we applied to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your body corporate applied to the Director?
      `the Director has determined that changing the reference is not practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director determined that it is not practicable to change a reference to the nominal or par value of shares of a class or series?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Director let us go on calling our shares par value shares` IF
    `the Director may permit continued reference to par value shares within s 187(11)` `we applied to the Director` `the Director has determined that changing the reference is not practicable`

@export Do our articles say what they must about the largest number of par value shares (s 187(12))?
GIVEN `we have been permitted to go on referring to par value shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been permitted, under section 187(11), to continue to refer to shares as having a nominal or par value?
      `the articles set out the maximum number of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your articles set out the maximum number of shares of the class or series?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do our articles say what they must about the largest number of par value shares` IF
    `the articles comply with the duty to set out the maximum number within s 187(12)` `we have been permitted to go on referring to par value shares` `the articles set out the maximum number of those shares`

@export May we amend our articles in this way, given our par value shares (s 187(12))?
GIVEN `we have been permitted to go on referring to par value shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been permitted, under section 187(11), to continue to refer to shares as having a nominal or par value?
      `the amendment raises the maximum number of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the amendment increase the maximum number of those shares?
      `the amendment changes the par value of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the amendment change the nominal or par value of those shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May we amend our articles in this way, given our par value shares` IF
    `the corporation may make the amendment within s 187(12)` `we have been permitted to go on referring to par value shares` `the amendment raises the maximum number of those shares` `the amendment changes the par value of those shares`

-- s 188(10). The other jurisdiction's laws must provide, in effect, all five.
@export May our corporation be continued under the laws of another jurisdiction (s 188(10))?
GIVEN `those laws keep our property as the new body corporate's` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the other jurisdiction's laws provide, in effect, that the corporation's property continues to be the property of the body corporate?
      `those laws keep the new body corporate liable for our obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they provide that the body corporate continues to be liable for the corporation's obligations?
      `those laws leave existing claims unaffected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they provide that an existing cause of action, claim or liability to prosecution is unaffected?
      `those laws let pending proceedings go on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they provide that a pending civil, criminal or administrative proceeding by or against the corporation may be continued by or against the body corporate?
      `those laws let judgments be enforced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they provide that a conviction, ruling, order or judgment may be enforced by or against the body corporate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our corporation be continued under the laws of another jurisdiction` IF
    `the corporation may be continued under the laws of another jurisdiction within s 188(10)` `those laws keep our property as the new body corporate's` `those laws keep the new body corporate liable for our obligations` `those laws leave existing claims unaffected` `those laws let pending proceedings go on` `those laws let judgments be enforced`

-- s 188(1).
@export May our corporation ask another jurisdiction to continue it there (s 188(1))?
GIVEN `the shareholders authorized the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the shareholders authorize the application in accordance with section 188?
      `we have satisfied the Director that creditors and shareholders will not be adversely affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you established, to the Director's satisfaction, that the proposed continuance will not adversely affect creditors or shareholders of the corporation?
      `the other jurisdiction's laws satisfy section 188(10)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the other jurisdiction's laws satisfy section 188(10)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our corporation ask another jurisdiction to continue it there` IF
    `the corporation may apply to another jurisdiction to be continued within s 188(1)` `the shareholders authorized the application` `we have satisfied the Director that creditors and shareholders will not be adversely affected` `the other jurisdiction's laws satisfy section 188(10)`

-- s 188(2). The other federal Acts: Bank Act, Canada Cooperatives Act, Cooperative Credit Associations Act,
-- Insurance Companies Act, Trust and Loan Companies Act.
@export May our corporation ask a Minister to continue it under one of the other federal Acts (s 188(2))?
GIVEN `the shareholders authorized the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the shareholders authorize the application in accordance with section 188?
      `the application is under one of those other Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application for continuance under the Bank Act, the Canada Cooperatives Act, the Cooperative Credit Associations Act, the Insurance Companies Act or the Trust and Loan Companies Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our corporation ask a Minister to continue it under one of the other federal Acts` IF
    `the corporation may apply to the appropriate Minister for continuance under another federal Act within s 188(2)` `the shareholders authorized the application` `the application is under one of those other Acts`

-- s 188(3). Section 135 says how a notice of a meeting is given.
@export Does the notice of the continuance meeting say what the Act requires (s 188(3))?
GIVEN `the notice complies with section 135` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice comply with section 135 (notice of a meeting of shareholders)?
      `the notice goes to every shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice sent to each shareholder?
      `shareholders have the right to dissent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a dissenting shareholder entitled under section 190 to be paid the fair value of their shares for this continuance?
      `the notice states that right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the notice of the continuance meeting say what the Act requires` IF
    `the notice of the meeting complies within s 188(3)` `the notice complies with section 135` `the notice goes to every shareholder` `shareholders have the right to dissent` `the notice states that right`

@export Is our departure invalid because the notice did not state my right to dissent (s 188(3))?
GIVEN `leaving out the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was leaving out the statement of the right to dissent the only thing wrong with the notice?
GIVETH A `Effect on validity of leaving out the dissent statement`
DECIDE `Is our departure invalid because the notice did not state my right to dissent` IS
    `the effect on the discontinuance of leaving out the dissent statement within s 188(3)` `leaving out the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice`

-- s 188(4).
@export Can I vote on the continuance elsewhere although my shares carry no other vote (s 188(4))?
GIVEN `my shares otherwise carry the right to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your shares otherwise carry the right to vote?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I vote on the continuance elsewhere although my shares carry no other vote` IF
    `the share carries the right to vote on the continuance within s 188(4)` `my shares otherwise carry the right to vote`

-- s 188(5).
@export Have the shareholders authorized the application for continuance (s 188(5))?
GIVEN `votes cast in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast in favour of the continuance by the shareholders who voted?
      `votes cast against` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast against it?
      `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have the shareholders authorized the application for continuance` IF
    `the application for continuance is authorized within s 188(5)` `our votes`
    WHERE
        `our votes` MEANS `Vote tally` WITH
            `votes cast in favour` IS `votes cast in favour`
            `votes cast against` IS `votes cast against`
            `signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on the resolution` IS `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote`

-- s 188(6).
@export May the directors drop the application without asking the shareholders again (s 188(6))?
GIVEN `the shareholders authorized abandonment when they approved the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When the shareholders approved the application, did they authorize the directors to abandon it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors drop the application without asking the shareholders again` IF
    `the directors may abandon the application without further approval of the shareholders within s 188(6)` `the shareholders authorized abandonment when they approved the application`

-- s 188(7), (8).
@export Must the Director file our notice of continuance elsewhere and give us a certificate of discontinuance (s 188(7))?
GIVEN `the Director has received our notice of continuance elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director received a notice that the corporation has been continued under the laws of another jurisdiction or under one of the other federal Acts?
      `the notice is satisfactory to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice satisfactory to the Director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director file our notice of continuance elsewhere and give us a certificate of discontinuance` IF
    `the Director must file the notice and issue a certificate of discontinuance within s 188(7)` `the Director has received our notice of continuance elsewhere` `the notice is satisfactory to the Director`

@export Is our notice of continuance elsewhere treated as articles in the form the Director fixes (s 188(8))?
GIVEN `the document is the notice referred to in section 188(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document the notice referred to in section 188(7)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our notice of continuance elsewhere treated as articles in the form the Director fixes` IF
    `the notice is deemed to be articles in the form the Director fixes for section 262 within s 188(8)` `the document is the notice referred to in section 188(7)`

-- s 188(9).
@export Does the Canada Business Corporations Act still govern us on the day I am asking about, after we left (s 188(9))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of discontinuance` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of discontinuance? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-01)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Canada Business Corporations Act still govern us on the day I am asking about, after we left` IF
    `this Act still applies to the corporation on a day within s 188(9)` `the date shown in the certificate of discontinuance` `the day I am asking about`

§§ `Borrowing, and selling the whole business (Part XV, s 189)`

-- s 189(1). Section 146 (piece cb3) defines a unanimous shareholder agreement.
@export May the directors do this without asking the shareholders (s 189(1))?
GIVEN `the power` IS A `Kind of financing power under s 189(1)` @desc What do the directors want to do? Choose the closest listed power, or "a power that s 189(1) does not list".
      `the articles otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the corporation's articles provide otherwise?
      `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the by-laws provide otherwise?
      `a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a unanimous shareholder agreement relating to the corporation provide otherwise?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors do this without asking the shareholders` IF
    `the directors may exercise the power without the shareholders' authorization within s 189(1)` `the power` `the articles otherwise provide` `the by-laws otherwise provide` `a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provides`

-- s 189(2).
@export May the directors hand their borrowing powers to someone else (s 189(2))?
GIVEN `the person who would receive them` IS A `Person to whom the borrowing powers are delegated (s 189(2))` @desc Who would receive the powers? Choose a director, a committee of directors, an officer, or "a person who is neither a director, a committee of directors nor an officer (s 189(2))".
      `the directors delegate by resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the directors delegate by resolution?
      `the articles otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the corporation's articles provide otherwise?
      `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the by-laws provide otherwise?
      `a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a unanimous shareholder agreement relating to the corporation provide otherwise?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors hand their borrowing powers to someone else` IF
    `the directors may delegate the powers in subsection 189(1) within s 189(2)` `the person who would receive them` `the directors delegate by resolution` `the articles otherwise provide` `the by-laws otherwise provide` `a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provides`

-- s 189(3).
@export Do the shareholders have to approve this sale, lease or exchange (s 189(3))?
GIVEN `it is of all or substantially all the corporation's property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sale, lease or exchange of all or substantially all the corporation's property?
      `it is outside the ordinary course of business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it other than in the ordinary course of business of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the shareholders have to approve this sale, lease or exchange` IF
    `the sale, lease or exchange needs the approval of the shareholders within s 189(3)` `it is of all or substantially all the corporation's property` `it is outside the ordinary course of business`

-- s 189(4).
@export Does the notice of the meeting on the sale say what the Act requires (s 189(4))?
GIVEN `the notice complies with section 135` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice comply with section 135 (notice of a meeting of shareholders)?
      `the notice goes to every shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice sent to each shareholder?
      `a copy or summary of the agreement is with the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice include, or come with, a copy or summary of the agreement of sale, lease or exchange?
      `shareholders have the right to dissent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a dissenting shareholder entitled under section 190 to be paid the fair value of their shares for this sale, lease or exchange?
      `the notice states that right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the notice of the meeting on the sale say what the Act requires` IF
    `the notice of the meeting complies within s 189(4)` `the notice complies with section 135` `the notice goes to every shareholder` `a copy or summary of the agreement is with the notice` `shareholders have the right to dissent` `the notice states that right`

@export Is the sale invalid because the notice did not state my right to dissent (s 189(4)(b))?
GIVEN `leaving out the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was leaving out the statement of the right to dissent the only thing wrong with the notice?
GIVETH A `Effect on validity of leaving out the dissent statement`
DECIDE `Is the sale invalid because the notice did not state my right to dissent` IS
    `the effect on the sale, lease or exchange of leaving out the dissent statement within s 189(4)(b)` `leaving out the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice`

-- s 189(5).
@export May the shareholders authorize the sale and fix, or leave to the directors, its terms (s 189(5))?
GIVEN `this is the meeting the notice under section 189(4) called` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the meeting referred to in section 189(4) (the meeting called by the notice)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the shareholders authorize the sale and fix, or leave to the directors, its terms` IF
    `the shareholders may authorize the sale, lease or exchange and fix or authorize the directors to fix its terms within s 189(5)` `this is the meeting the notice under section 189(4) called`

-- s 189(6).
@export Can I vote on the sale although my shares carry no other vote (s 189(6))?
GIVEN `my shares otherwise carry the right to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your shares otherwise carry the right to vote?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I vote on the sale although my shares carry no other vote` IF
    `the share carries the right to vote on the sale, lease or exchange within s 189(6)` `my shares otherwise carry the right to vote`

-- s 189(7).
@export Does my class or series vote separately on the sale (s 189(7))?
GIVEN `my class or series is affected in a manner different from the shares of another class or series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your class or series affected by the sale, lease or exchange in a manner different from the shares of another class or series?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my class or series vote separately on the sale` IF
    `the holders of a class or series are entitled to vote separately on the sale, lease or exchange within s 189(7)` `my class or series is affected in a manner different from the shares of another class or series`

-- s 189(8).
@export Have the shareholders adopted the sale, lease or exchange (s 189(8))?
GIVEN `votes cast in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast in favour of the sale, lease or exchange by the shareholders who voted?
      `votes cast against` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast against it?
      `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on it?
      `every class or series with a separate vote approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If any class or series had a separate vote, did each one approve by special resolution? Answer yes if none had a separate vote.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have the shareholders adopted the sale, lease or exchange` IF
    `the sale, lease or exchange is adopted within s 189(8)` `our votes` `every class or series with a separate vote approved`
    WHERE
        `our votes` MEANS `Vote tally` WITH
            `votes cast in favour` IS `votes cast in favour`
            `votes cast against` IS `votes cast against`
            `signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on the resolution` IS `the resolution was signed by every shareholder entitled to vote`

-- s 189(9).
@export May the directors drop an approved sale without asking the shareholders again (s 189(9))?
GIVEN `the shareholders authorized abandonment when they approved the sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When the shareholders approved the sale, lease or exchange, did they authorize the directors to abandon it?
      `abandoning it would defeat a right of a third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would abandoning it defeat a right of a third party?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors drop an approved sale without asking the shareholders again` IF
    `the directors may abandon the sale, lease or exchange without further approval of the shareholders within s 189(9)` `the shareholders authorized abandonment when they approved the sale` `abandoning it would defeat a right of a third party`

§§ `Dissenting: asking the corporation to buy my shares (Part XV, s 190)`

-- A shareholder who objects to a fundamental change may insist that the corporation buy their shares at
-- "fair value". The steps run against the clock: each deadline has a question for its last day and, where
-- it matters, a question for whether a given day is in time. A period of N days counts the day it runs
-- from as day 0 and includes day N.

-- s 190(1).
@export May I dissent from what my corporation is doing (s 190(1))?
GIVEN `what the corporation is doing` IS AN `Action that gives a right to dissent under s 190(1)` @desc What is the corporation doing? Choose the closest listed action, or "an action that s 190(1) does not list".
      `the provisions concern my class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is amending the articles to restrict or constrain the issue, transfer or ownership of shares: do the provisions concern shares of your class?
      `the amendment is made under section 191 (court-ordered reorganization)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amendment made under section 191 (a reorganization by court order)?
      `section 241 displaces the right to dissent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 241 (an oppression-remedy order) displace the right to dissent here?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I dissent from what my corporation is doing` IF
    `a holder of shares of a class may dissent within s 190(1)` `what the corporation is doing` `the provisions concern my class of shares` `the amendment is made under section 191 (court-ordered reorganization)` `section 241 displaces the right to dissent`

-- s 190(2). The class vote is the one s 176 gives.
@export May I dissent from an amendment because my class or series has a separate vote on it (s 190(2))?
GIVEN `what the amendment does to my class` IS AN `Effect of a proposed amendment on a class of shares (s 176(1))` @desc What does the amendment do to your class? Choose the closest listed effect, or "no effect that s 176(1) lists".
      `the articles say my class has no separate vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles provide that the holders of your class may not vote separately? (Matters only for some effects.)
      `the new class is constrained and otherwise equal to mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the new class one whose issue, transfer or ownership is constrained under paragraph 174(1)(c) and which is otherwise equal to your class?
      `the amendment only adds a right to convert into such a class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the amendment only add a right to convert shares into an otherwise equal class that is constrained under paragraph 174(1)(c)?
      `my shares are a series of a class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold shares of a series of a class?
      `my series is affected differently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your series affected differently from the other shares of the same class?
      `the corporation has resolved to amend its articles in that way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation resolved to amend its articles in that way?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I dissent from an amendment because my class or series has a separate vote on it` IF
    `a holder of shares of a class or series may dissent within s 190(2)`
        (`the holders of a class or series are entitled to vote separately within s 176(1) and s 176(4)` `what the amendment does to my class` `the articles say my class has no separate vote` `the new class is constrained and otherwise equal to mine` `the amendment only adds a right to convert into such a class` `my shares are a series of a class` `my series is affected differently`)
        `the corporation has resolved to amend its articles in that way`

@export Can I dissent even though my corporation has only one class of shares (s 190(2.1))?
GIVEN `my corporation has only one class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your corporation have only one class of shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I dissent even though my corporation has only one class of shares` IF
    `the right in subsection 190(2) applies whatever the number of classes within s 190(2.1)` `my corporation has only one class of shares`

-- s 190(3). "A shareholder who complies with this section" is one who took every step below.
@export Am I entitled to be paid the fair value of my shares (s 190(3))?
GIVEN `my claim covers all the shares as subsection 190(4) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your claim cover all the shares of the class held for one beneficial owner and registered in your name?
      `I met the objection requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you send the written objection at or before the meeting (or did the corporation fail to give notice of the meeting's purpose and your right to dissent)?
      `my demand for payment was in time and complete` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you send your demand for payment within twenty days, containing your name and address, the number and class of shares and the demand?
      `my certificates were sent in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you send your share certificates within thirty days after sending your demand?
      `the action or order has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the action approved by the resolution, or the court order, become effective?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to be paid the fair value of my shares` IF
    `the dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of the shares within s 190(3)`
        (`the shareholder has taken every step of s 190` `my claim covers all the shares as subsection 190(4) requires` `I met the objection requirement` `my demand for payment was in time and complete` `my certificates were sent in time`)
        `the action or order has become effective`

@export As of what day is the fair value of my shares determined (s 190(3))?
GIVEN `the day the resolution was adopted or the order was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the resolution adopted, or the order made? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `As of what day is the fair value of my shares determined` IS
    `the day as of which fair value is determined within s 190(3)` `the day the resolution was adopted or the order was made`

-- s 190(4).
@export Does my claim cover the right number of shares (s 190(4))?
GIVEN `the number of shares of the class that my claim covers` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of the class does your claim cover?
      `the number of shares of the class held for that beneficial owner and registered in my name` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of the class are held on behalf of that one beneficial owner and registered in your name?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my claim cover the right number of shares` IF
    `the claim is permitted within s 190(4)` `the number of shares of the class that my claim covers` `the number of shares of the class held for that beneficial owner and registered in my name`

-- s 190(5).
@export Have I met the requirement to object in writing (s 190(5))?
GIVEN `I sent the corporation a written objection at or before the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you send the corporation a written objection at or before the meeting at which the resolution was to be voted on?
      `the corporation gave me no notice of the meeting's purpose and my right to dissent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation fail to give you notice of the purpose of the meeting and of your right to dissent?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met the requirement to object in writing` IF
    `the objection requirement is satisfied within s 190(5)` `I sent the corporation a written objection at or before the meeting` `the corporation gave me no notice of the meeting's purpose and my right to dissent`

-- s 190(6).
@export Must the corporation send me notice that the resolution has been adopted (s 190(6))?
GIVEN `I filed an objection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file the written objection referred to in section 190(5)?
      `I voted for the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you vote for the resolution?
      `I withdrew my objection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you withdraw your objection?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation send me notice that the resolution has been adopted` IF
    `the corporation must send the shareholder notice that the resolution has been adopted within s 190(6)` `I filed an objection` `I voted for the resolution` `I withdrew my objection`

@export By what day must the corporation send me notice that the resolution was adopted (s 190(6))?
GIVEN `the day the shareholders adopted the resolution` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the shareholders adopt the resolution? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the corporation send me notice that the resolution was adopted` IS
    `the last day for the corporation to send the notice of adoption within s 190(6)` `the day the shareholders adopted the resolution`

@export Did the corporation send me notice that the resolution was adopted in time (s 190(6))?
GIVEN `the day the shareholders adopted the resolution` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the shareholders adopt the resolution? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-01)
      `the day the corporation sent the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the corporation send the notice? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-11)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the corporation send me notice that the resolution was adopted in time` IF
    `the notice of adoption was sent in time within s 190(6)` `the day the shareholders adopted the resolution` `the day the corporation sent the notice`

-- s 190(7).
@export By what day must I send my demand for payment (s 190(7))?
GIVEN `I received a notice under subsection 190(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive the corporation's notice that the resolution was adopted (section 190(6))?
      `the day I received that notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you receive it? (ISO 8601; any date if you did not receive it)
      `the day I learned that the resolution had been adopted` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you learn that the resolution had been adopted? (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I send my demand for payment` IS
    `the last day for the shareholder to send the demand for payment within s 190(7)` (`the day the twenty days for the demand for payment start within s 190(7)` `I received a notice under subsection 190(6)` `the day I received that notice` `the day I learned that the resolution had been adopted`)

@export Did I send my demand for payment in time (s 190(7))?
GIVEN `I received a notice under subsection 190(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive the corporation's notice that the resolution was adopted (section 190(6))?
      `the day I received that notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you receive it? (ISO 8601; any date if you did not receive it)
      `the day I learned that the resolution had been adopted` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you learn that the resolution had been adopted? (ISO 8601)
      `the day I sent my demand` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you send your demand for payment? (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I send my demand for payment in time` IF
    `the demand for payment was sent in time within s 190(7)` (`the day the twenty days for the demand for payment start within s 190(7)` `I received a notice under subsection 190(6)` `the day I received that notice` `the day I learned that the resolution had been adopted`) `the day I sent my demand`

@export Does my demand for payment say everything the Act requires (s 190(7))?
GIVEN `it contains my name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your notice contain your name and address?
      `it contains the number and class of my shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain the number and class of shares in respect of which you dissent?
      `it demands payment of the fair value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain a demand for payment of the fair value of those shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my demand for payment say everything the Act requires` IF
    `the notice contains what s 190(7) requires` `it contains my name and address` `it contains the number and class of my shares` `it demands payment of the fair value`

-- s 190(8) to (10).
@export By what day must I send in my share certificates (s 190(8))?
GIVEN `the day I sent my demand for payment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you send your demand for payment? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-04-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I send in my share certificates` IS
    `the last day for the shareholder to send the certificates within s 190(8)` `the day I sent my demand for payment`

@export Did I send in my share certificates in time (s 190(8))?
GIVEN `the day I sent my demand for payment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you send your demand for payment? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-04-01)
      `the day I sent my certificates` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you send your certificates? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-05-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I send in my share certificates in time` IF
    `the certificates were sent in time within s 190(8)` `the day I sent my demand for payment` `the day I sent my certificates`

@export Do I lose my claim because I did not send my certificates properly (s 190(9))?
GIVEN `I complied with subsection 190(8)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you comply with section 190(8) (sending your certificates in time)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I lose my claim because I did not send my certificates properly` IF
    `the shareholder is barred from making a claim within s 190(9)` `I complied with subsection 190(8)`

@export Must the corporation endorse my certificate and give it back to me (s 190(10))?
GIVEN `the corporation or its transfer agent received my certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation or its transfer agent received your share certificate under section 190(8)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation endorse my certificate and give it back to me` IF
    `the corporation or its transfer agent must endorse the certificate and return it within s 190(10)` `the corporation or its transfer agent received my certificate`

-- s 190(11).
@export Am I left with only the right to be paid for my shares (s 190(11))?
GIVEN `I have sent a demand for payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you sent your notice under section 190(7)?
      `I withdrew it before the corporation made an offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you withdraw it before the corporation made an offer under section 190(12)?
      `the corporation failed to make an offer in accordance with section 190(12)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation fail to make an offer in accordance with section 190(12)?
      `I withdrew it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you withdraw the notice?
      `the directors called the action off` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors revoke the resolution, terminate the amalgamation agreement or the application for continuance, or abandon the sale, lease or exchange?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I left with only the right to be paid for my shares` IF
    `the shareholder has no rights as a shareholder other than to be paid within s 190(11)` `I have sent a demand for payment` `I withdrew it before the corporation made an offer` `the corporation failed to make an offer in accordance with section 190(12)` `I withdrew it` `the directors called the action off`

@export Have my rights as a shareholder been restored (s 190(11))?
GIVEN `I have sent a demand for payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you sent your notice under section 190(7)?
      `I withdrew it before the corporation made an offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you withdraw it before the corporation made an offer under section 190(12)?
      `the corporation failed to make an offer in accordance with section 190(12)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation fail to make an offer in accordance with section 190(12)?
      `I withdrew it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you withdraw the notice?
      `the directors called the action off` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors revoke the resolution, terminate the amalgamation agreement or the application for continuance, or abandon the sale, lease or exchange?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have my rights as a shareholder been restored` IF
    `the shareholder's rights as a shareholder are reinstated within s 190(11)` `I have sent a demand for payment` `I withdrew it before the corporation made an offer` `the corporation failed to make an offer in accordance with section 190(12)` `I withdrew it` `the directors called the action off`

@export From what day do my restored rights count (s 190(11))?
GIVEN `the day I sent my demand for payment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you send your notice under section 190(7)? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-04-01)
      `my rights have been restored` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have your rights as a shareholder been restored under section 190(11)?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From what day do my restored rights count` IS
    `the day from which the reinstated rights count within s 190(11)` `the day I sent my demand for payment` `my rights have been restored`

-- s 190(12) to (14).
@export By what day must the corporation make me an offer (s 190(12))?
GIVEN `the day the action became effective` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the action approved by the resolution become effective? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-04-10)
      `the day the corporation received my demand for payment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the corporation receive your notice under section 190(7)? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-04-04)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the corporation make me an offer` IS
    `the last day for the corporation to send the offer within s 190(12)` (`the day the seven days for the offer start within s 190(12)` `the day the action became effective` `the day the corporation received my demand for payment`)

@export Did the corporation make me an offer in time (s 190(12))?
GIVEN `the day the action became effective` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the action approved by the resolution become effective? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-04-10)
      `the day the corporation received my demand for payment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the corporation receive your notice under section 190(7)? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-04-04)
      `the day the corporation sent its offer or notification` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the corporation send its offer or its notification? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-04-17)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the corporation make me an offer in time` IF
    `the offer or notification was sent in time within s 190(12)` (`the day the seven days for the offer start within s 190(12)` `the day the action became effective` `the day the corporation received my demand for payment`) `the day the corporation sent its offer or notification`

@export Did the corporation respond to my demand as the Act requires (s 190(12))?
GIVEN `the corporation sent a written offer to pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation send you a written offer to pay for your shares?
      `the offer is for what the directors consider the fair value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer for an amount the directors consider to be the fair value?
      `the offer has a statement of how the fair value was determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer accompanied by a statement showing how the fair value was determined?
      `the corporation says it may not lawfully pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 190(26) apply (are there reasonable grounds to believe it cannot lawfully pay)?
      `the corporation sent a notification that it is unable to pay lawfully` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation send a notification that it is unable lawfully to pay dissenting shareholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the corporation respond to my demand as the Act requires` IF
    `the corporation's response to the dissenting shareholder complies with s 190(12)` `the corporation sent a written offer to pay` `the offer is for what the directors consider the fair value` `the offer has a statement of how the fair value was determined` `the corporation says it may not lawfully pay` `the corporation sent a notification that it is unable to pay lawfully`

@export Are the corporation's offers to holders of my class on the same terms (s 190(13))?
GIVEN `the offers are for shares of the same class or series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the offers for shares of the same class or series?
      `the offers are on the same terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the offers on the same terms?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the corporation's offers to holders of my class on the same terms` IF
    `the offers comply with s 190(13)` `the offers are for shares of the same class or series` `the offers are on the same terms`

@export Must the corporation pay me for my shares now (s 190(14))?
GIVEN `I have accepted the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you accepted the corporation's offer (and has the corporation received your acceptance)?
      `the corporation may not lawfully pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 190(26) apply (are there reasonable grounds to believe the corporation cannot lawfully pay)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation pay me for my shares now` IF
    `the corporation must pay for the shares within s 190(14)` `I have accepted the offer` `the corporation may not lawfully pay`

@export By what day must the corporation pay me after I accept its offer (s 190(14))?
GIVEN `the day I accepted the offer` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the offer get accepted? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-04-20)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the corporation pay me after I accept its offer` IS
    `the last day for the corporation to pay within s 190(14)` `the day I accepted the offer`

@export Did the corporation pay me in time (s 190(14))?
GIVEN `the day I accepted the offer` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the offer get accepted? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-04-20)
      `the day the corporation paid me` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the corporation pay you? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-04-30)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the corporation pay me in time` IF
    `the payment was made in time within s 190(14)` `the day I accepted the offer` `the day the corporation paid me`

@export By what day must the corporation receive my acceptance of its offer (s 190(14))?
GIVEN `the day the corporation made me the offer` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the corporation make you the offer? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-04-17)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the corporation receive my acceptance of its offer` IS
    `the last day for the corporation to receive an acceptance within s 190(14)` `the day the corporation made me the offer`

@export Has the corporation's offer lapsed on the day I am asking about (s 190(14))?
GIVEN `the day the corporation made me the offer` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the corporation make you the offer? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-04-17)
      `the corporation has received an acceptance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation received an acceptance of the offer?
      `the day the corporation received my acceptance` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the corporation receive the acceptance? (ISO 8601; any date if it has not)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-05-18)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation's offer lapsed on the day I am asking about` IF
    `the offer has lapsed on a day within s 190(14)` `the day the corporation made me the offer` `the corporation has received an acceptance` `the day the corporation received my acceptance` `the day I am asking about`

-- s 190(15) to (19).
@export May the corporation ask a court to fix the value of my shares (s 190(15))?
GIVEN `the corporation failed to make an offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation fail to make an offer under section 190(12)?
      `I failed to accept an offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the dissenting shareholder fail to accept an offer?
      `the day the action became effective` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the action approved by the resolution become effective? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-01)
      `the day the corporation applied to the court` IS A DATE @desc On what day did (or will) the corporation apply to the court? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-21)
      `a court has allowed a further period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court allowed a further period?
      `the last day of the further period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of that further period? (ISO 8601; any date if none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation ask a court to fix the value of my shares` IF
    `the corporation may apply to a court to fix a fair value within s 190(15)` `the corporation failed to make an offer` `I failed to accept an offer` `the day the action became effective` `the day the corporation applied to the court` `a court has allowed a further period` `the last day of the further period`

@export By what day may the corporation ask a court to fix the value (s 190(15))?
GIVEN `the day the action became effective` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the action approved by the resolution become effective? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day may the corporation ask a court to fix the value` IS
    `the last day for the corporation to apply to a court within s 190(15)` `the day the action became effective`

@export May I ask a court to fix the value of my shares myself (s 190(16))?
GIVEN `the corporation failed to apply to a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation fail to apply to a court under section 190(15)?
      `the day the action became effective` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the action approved by the resolution become effective? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-01)
      `the day I apply to the court` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you apply (or did you apply) to the court? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-08-10)
      `a court has allowed me a further period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court allowed a further period?
      `the last day of the further period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of that further period? (ISO 8601; any date if none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask a court to fix the value of my shares myself` IF
    `the dissenting shareholder may apply to a court to fix a fair value within s 190(16)` `the corporation failed to apply to a court` `the day the action became effective` `the day I apply to the court` `a court has allowed me a further period` `the last day of the further period`

@export By what day may I ask a court to fix the value of my shares (s 190(16))?
GIVEN `the day the action became effective` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the action approved by the resolution become effective? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day may I ask a court to fix the value of my shares` IS
    `the last day for the dissenting shareholder to apply to a court within s 190(16)` `the day the action became effective`

@export Is this the right court to apply to (s 190(17))?
GIVEN `it has jurisdiction where the corporation has its registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court have jurisdiction in the place where the corporation has its registered office?
      `it has jurisdiction in the province where I live` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court have jurisdiction in the province where the dissenting shareholder resides?
      `the corporation carries on business in my province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation carry on business in that province?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this the right court to apply to` IF
    `the court is a proper court within s 190(17)` `it has jurisdiction where the corporation has its registered office` `it has jurisdiction in the province where I live` `the corporation carries on business in my province`

@export Must I give security for costs when I apply to the court (s 190(18))?
GIVEN `the application is under subsection 190(15) or 190(16)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made under section 190(15) or 190(16)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give security for costs when I apply to the court` IS
    `a dissenting shareholder is required to give security for costs within s 190(18)` `the application is under subsection 190(15) or 190(16)`

@export Will I be a party to the court application and bound by its decision (s 190(19))?
GIVEN `the corporation has not purchased my shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation not yet purchased your shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will I be a party to the court application and bound by its decision` IF
    `the dissenting shareholder must be joined as a party and is bound by the decision within s 190(19)(a)` `the corporation has not purchased my shares`

@export Has the corporation told me what it must about the court application (s 190(19))?
GIVEN `its notice states the date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation's notice state the date of the application?
      `its notice states the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the place of the application?
      `its notice states the consequences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the consequences of the application?
      `its notice states my right to appear and be heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state your right to appear and be heard in person or by counsel?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation told me what it must about the court application` IF
    `the corporation's notice to the dissenting shareholder complies with s 190(19)(b)` `its notice states the date` `its notice states the place` `its notice states the consequences` `its notice states my right to appear and be heard`

-- s 190(20) to (23). The court's powers, asked for what they mean to the shareholder.
@export Will the court fix a fair value for the shares of all dissenting shareholders together (s 190(20))?
GIVEN `an application has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made to a court under section 190(15) or 190(16)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the court fix a fair value for the shares of all dissenting shareholders together` IF
    `the court must fix a fair value for the shares of all dissenting shareholders within s 190(20)` `an application has been made`

@export May the court appoint appraisers to help fix the value (s 190(21))?
GIVEN `an application has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made to a court under section 190(15) or 190(16)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court appoint appraisers to help fix the value` IF
    `the court may appoint appraisers within s 190(21)` `an application has been made`

@export Will the court's final order be against the corporation and in my favour (s 190(22))?
GIVEN `the court has fixed a fair value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court fixed a fair value for the shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the court's final order be against the corporation and in my favour` IF
    `the final order is rendered against the corporation in favour of each dissenting shareholder within s 190(22)` `the court has fixed a fair value`

@export May the court allow interest on what I am owed for the day I am asking about (s 190(23))?
GIVEN `the day the action became effective` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the action approved by the resolution become effective? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-01)
      `the day of payment` IS A DATE @desc On what day was (or will) the payment be made? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-30)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-15)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court allow interest on what I am owed for the day I am asking about` IF
    `the court may allow interest for a day within s 190(23)` `the day the action became effective` `the day of payment` `the day I am asking about`

-- s 190(24) to (26).
@export Must the corporation tell me it cannot lawfully pay (s 190(24))?
GIVEN `section 190(26) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 190(26) apply (are there reasonable grounds to believe the corporation cannot lawfully pay)?
      `a court has pronounced a final order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court pronounced an order under section 190(22)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation tell me it cannot lawfully pay` IF
    `the corporation must notify each dissenting shareholder that it is unable lawfully to pay within s 190(24)` `section 190(26) applies` `a court has pronounced a final order`

@export By what day must the corporation tell me it cannot lawfully pay (s 190(24))?
GIVEN `the day the court pronounced the order` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the court pronounce the order? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-08-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the corporation tell me it cannot lawfully pay` IS
    `the last day for the corporation to give the notice within s 190(24)` `the day the court pronounced the order`

@export Did the corporation tell me in time that it cannot lawfully pay (s 190(24))?
GIVEN `the day the court pronounced the order` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the court pronounce the order? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-08-01)
      `the day the corporation gave me the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the corporation give you the notice? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-08-11)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the corporation tell me in time that it cannot lawfully pay` IF
    `the notice was given in time within s 190(24)` `the day the court pronounced the order` `the day the corporation gave me the notice`

@export By what day must I answer the corporation's notice that it cannot pay (s 190(25))?
GIVEN `the day I received the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you receive the corporation's notice under section 190(24)? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-08-15)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I answer the corporation's notice that it cannot pay` IS
    `the last day for the shareholder to deliver the written notice within s 190(25)` `the day I received the notice`

@export Did I answer the corporation's notice that it cannot pay in time (s 190(25))?
GIVEN `the day I received the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you receive the corporation's notice under section 190(24)? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-08-15)
      `the day I delivered my written notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you deliver your written notice? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-09-14)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I answer the corporation's notice that it cannot pay in time` IF
    `the written notice was delivered in time within s 190(25)` `the day I received the notice` `the day I delivered my written notice`

@export What happens if I withdraw my dissent, or stay on as a claimant (s 190(25))?
GIVEN `section 190(26) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 190(26) apply?
      `I delivered my written notice in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deliver your written notice within thirty days after receiving the corporation's notice?
      `my choice` IS A `Choice of a dissenting shareholder under s 190(25)` @desc What did you choose: to withdraw your notice of dissent, or to retain a status as a claimant against the corporation?
GIVETH A `Effect of the choice of a dissenting shareholder under s 190(25)`
DECIDE `What happens if I withdraw my dissent, or stay on as a claimant` IS
    `the effect of the shareholder's choice within s 190(25)` `section 190(26) applies` `I delivered my written notice in time` `my choice`

@export Must the corporation refuse to pay me because it cannot lawfully do so (s 190(26))?
GIVEN `it is or would after the payment be unable to pay its liabilities as they become due` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation is, or would after the payment be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due?
      `the realizable value of its assets would thereby be less than its liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds for believing that the realizable value of the corporation's assets would thereby be less than the aggregate of its liabilities?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation refuse to pay me because it cannot lawfully do so` IF
    `the corporation must not make a payment to a dissenting shareholder within s 190(26)` `it is or would after the payment be unable to pay its liabilities as they become due` `the realizable value of its assets would thereby be less than its liabilities`

§§ `Court-ordered reorganization and arrangement (Part XV, ss 191 and 192)`

-- A "reorganization" is a court order under the oppression remedy, the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act or
-- another federal Act. An "arrangement" is a fundamental change a solvent corporation puts to the court
-- when no other provision of the Act can practicably be used.

-- s 191(1).
@export Is this court order a reorganization under the Act (s 191(1))?
GIVEN `the kind of order` IS A `Kind of court order for s 191(1)` @desc What kind of court order is it? Choose the closest listed kind, or "an order that is none of these".
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this court order a reorganization under the Act` IF
    `the order is a reorganization within s 191(1)` `the kind of order`

-- s 191(2), (3).
@export May the court's order amend our articles in this way (s 191(2))?
GIVEN `our corporation is subject to a reorganization order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation subject to an order referred to in section 191(1)?
      `the change is one an amendment under section 173 could lawfully make` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change one that might lawfully be made by an amendment under section 173?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court's order amend our articles in this way` IF
    `the order may amend the articles to effect the change within s 191(2)` `our corporation is subject to a reorganization order` `the change is one an amendment under section 173 could lawfully make`

@export May the court authorize our corporation to issue debt obligations and fix their terms (s 191(3)(a))?
GIVEN `a court has made a reorganization order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court made an order referred to in section 191(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court authorize our corporation to issue debt obligations and fix their terms` IF
    `the court may authorize the issue of debt obligations and fix their terms within s 191(3)(a)` `a court has made a reorganization order`

@export May the court replace or add to our directors (s 191(3)(b))?
GIVEN `a court has made a reorganization order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court made an order referred to in section 191(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court replace or add to our directors` IF
    `the court may appoint directors in place of or in addition to those in office within s 191(3)(b)` `a court has made a reorganization order`

-- s 191(4) to (7).
@export Must we send articles of reorganization to the Director (s 191(4))?
GIVEN `a reorganization order has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an order referred to in section 191(1) been made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must we send articles of reorganization to the Director` IF
    `the corporation must send articles of reorganization to the Director within s 191(4)` `a reorganization order has been made`

@export Have we sent our articles of reorganization to the Director as the Act requires (s 191(4))?
GIVEN `the articles are in the form the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the articles of reorganization in the form the Director fixes?
      `sections 19 and 113 call for documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do sections 19 and 113 call for documents to be sent with the articles ("if applicable")?
      `we sent those documents with them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you send those documents with the articles?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have we sent our articles of reorganization to the Director as the Act requires` IF
    `the articles of reorganization have been sent as s 191(4) requires` `the articles are in the form the Director fixes` `sections 19 and 113 call for documents` `we sent those documents with them`

@export Must the Director give us a certificate of amendment for our reorganization (s 191(5))?
GIVEN `the Director has received our articles of reorganization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director received the articles of reorganization?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director give us a certificate of amendment for our reorganization` IF
    `the Director must issue a certificate of amendment within s 191(5)` `the Director has received our articles of reorganization`

@export Has our reorganization taken effect on the day I am asking about (s 191(6))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amendment` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of amendment? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-09-01)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-09-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has our reorganization taken effect on the day I am asking about` IF
    `the reorganization is effective and the articles are amended on a day within s 191(6)` `the date shown in the certificate of amendment` `the day I am asking about`

@export Am I shut out of dissenting because the amendment was made by a reorganization order (s 191(7))?
GIVEN `the amendment to the articles was effected under section 191` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the amendment to the articles effected under section 191?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I shut out of dissenting because the amendment was made by a reorganization order` IF
    `a shareholder is not entitled to dissent under section 190 within s 191(7)` `the amendment to the articles was effected under section 191`

-- s 192(1) to (3).
@export Is this transaction an "arrangement" under the Act (s 192(1))?
GIVEN `the kind of transaction` IS A `Kind of transaction named in s 192(1)` @desc What kind of transaction is it? Choose the closest named kind, or "a transaction that is not named in s 192(1)".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this transaction an "arrangement" under the Act` IS
    `whether the transaction is an arrangement within s 192(1)` `the kind of transaction`

@export Is my corporation insolvent under the Act (s 192(2))?
GIVEN `we are unable to pay our liabilities as they become due` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation unable to pay its liabilities as they become due?
      `the realizable value of our assets` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the realizable value of the corporation's assets, in dollars?
      `the aggregate of our liabilities` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the corporation's liabilities, in dollars?
      `the stated capital of all our classes` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the stated capital of all classes of the corporation's shares, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation insolvent under the Act` IF
    `the corporation is insolvent within s 192(2)` `we are unable to pay our liabilities as they become due` `the realizable value of our assets` `the aggregate of our liabilities` `the stated capital of all our classes`

@export May my corporation ask a court to approve an arrangement (s 192(3))?
GIVEN `we are unable to pay our liabilities as they become due` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation unable to pay its liabilities as they become due?
      `the realizable value of our assets` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the realizable value of the corporation's assets, in dollars?
      `the aggregate of our liabilities` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the corporation's liabilities, in dollars?
      `the stated capital of all our classes` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the stated capital of all classes of the corporation's shares, in dollars?
      `it is not practicable to make the change under another provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it not practicable to effect the fundamental change under any other provision of the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation ask a court to approve an arrangement` IF
    `the corporation may apply to a court for an order approving an arrangement within s 192(3)` (`the corporation is insolvent within s 192(2)` `we are unable to pay our liabilities as they become due` `the realizable value of our assets` `the aggregate of our liabilities` `the stated capital of all our classes`) `it is not practicable to make the change under another provision`

-- s 192(4).
@export May the court make this order on our application (s 192(4))?
GIVEN `an application has been made under section 192` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made under section 192?
      `the court thinks the order fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court think the order fit?
      `the order` IS A `Kind of order under s 192(4)` @desc What order is sought? Choose the closest listed kind, or "any other interim or final order the court thinks fit".
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court make this order on our application` IF
    `the court may make the order within s 192(4)` `an application has been made under section 192` `the court thinks the order fit` `the order`

-- s 192(5).
@export Must we give the Director notice of our application to the court (s 192(5))?
GIVEN `we have applied for an interim or final order under section 192` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for an interim or final order under section 192?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must we give the Director notice of our application to the court` IF
    `the applicant must give the Director notice of the application within s 192(5)` `we have applied for an interim or final order under section 192`

@export Is the Director entitled to appear and be heard on the application (s 192(5))?
GIVEN `an application for an interim or final order under section 192 has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application for an interim or final order under section 192 been made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Director entitled to appear and be heard on the application` IF
    `the Director is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel within s 192(5)` `an application for an interim or final order under section 192 has been made`

-- s 192(6) to (8).
@export Must we send articles of arrangement to the Director (s 192(6))?
GIVEN `the court has approved the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an order approving the arrangement (paragraph 192(4)(e)) been made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must we send articles of arrangement to the Director` IF
    `the corporation must send articles of arrangement to the Director within s 192(6)` `the court has approved the arrangement`

@export Have we sent our articles of arrangement to the Director as the Act requires (s 192(6))?
GIVEN `the articles are in the form the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the articles of arrangement in the form the Director fixes?
      `sections 19 and 113 call for documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do sections 19 and 113 call for documents to be sent with the articles ("if applicable")?
      `we sent those documents with them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you send those documents with the articles?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have we sent our articles of arrangement to the Director as the Act requires` IF
    `the articles of arrangement have been sent as s 192(6) requires` `the articles are in the form the Director fixes` `sections 19 and 113 call for documents` `we sent those documents with them`

@export Must the Director give us a certificate of arrangement (s 192(7))?
GIVEN `the Director has received our articles of arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director received the articles of arrangement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director give us a certificate of arrangement` IF
    `the Director must issue a certificate of arrangement within s 192(7)` `the Director has received our articles of arrangement`

@export Has our arrangement taken effect on the day I am asking about (s 192(8))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of arrangement` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of arrangement? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-10-01)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-10-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has our arrangement taken effect on the day I am asking about` IF
    `the arrangement is effective on a day within s 192(8)` `the date shown in the certificate of arrangement` `the day I am asking about`

§§ `Going private and squeeze-outs (Part XVI, ss 193 and 194)`

-- A "squeeze-out transaction" ends a holder's interest without their consent. "Going-private transaction"
-- is defined by the regulations, which are not among the sources.

-- s 2(1), asked because s 194 turns on it.
@export Is this a squeeze-out transaction (s 2(1))?
GIVEN `the transaction is by a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction by a corporation?
      `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a distributing corporation?
      `the transaction would require an amendment to the corporation's articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the transaction require an amendment to the corporation's articles?
      `the transaction would terminate a holder's interest without their consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the transaction, directly or indirectly, terminate the interest of a holder of shares of a class without the holder's consent?
      `an interest of equivalent value is substituted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an interest of equivalent value substituted?
      `the substituted interest is in shares issued by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the substituted interest in shares issued by the corporation?
      `those shares have equal or greater rights and privileges` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do those shares have equal or greater rights and privileges than the shares of the affected class?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a squeeze-out transaction` IF
    `squeeze-out transaction within s 2(1)` `the transaction is by a corporation` `the corporation is a distributing corporation` `the transaction would require an amendment to the corporation's articles` `the transaction would terminate a holder's interest without their consent` `an interest of equivalent value is substituted` `the substituted interest is in shares issued by the corporation` `those shares have equal or greater rights and privileges`

-- s 193.
@export May my corporation carry out a going-private transaction (s 193)?
GIVEN `there are applicable provincial securities laws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there any applicable provincial securities laws?
      `our corporation complies with those laws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your corporation comply with those laws?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation carry out a going-private transaction` IF
    `a corporation may carry out a going-private transaction within s 193` `there are applicable provincial securities laws` `our corporation complies with those laws`

-- s 194.
@export May I vote on the squeeze-out resolution (s 194)?
GIVEN `my shares otherwise carry the right to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your shares otherwise carry the right to vote?
      `I am an affiliate of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an affiliate of the corporation?
      `I would get greater value or superior rights than other holders of my class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After the squeeze-out transaction, would you be entitled to consideration of greater value, or to superior rights or privileges, than other holders of shares of your class?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I vote on the squeeze-out resolution` IF
    `the holder may vote on the squeeze-out resolution within s 194` `my shares otherwise carry the right to vote` `I am an affiliate of the corporation` `I would get greater value or superior rights than other holders of my class`

@export Has my class approved the squeeze-out transaction by ordinary resolution (s 194)?
GIVEN `votes cast in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes did the eligible holders of your class cast in favour?
      `votes cast against` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes did they cast against? (A resolution in writing signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote, section 142(1)(a), is not modelled by this question.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my class approved the squeeze-out transaction by ordinary resolution` IF
    `the holders of a class have approved the squeeze-out transaction within s 194` `my class's votes`
    WHERE
        `my class's votes` MEANS `Vote tally` WITH
            `votes cast in favour` IS `votes cast in favour`
            `votes cast against` IS `votes cast against`
            `signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on the resolution` IS FALSE

@export May my corporation carry out this squeeze-out transaction (s 194)?
GIVEN `it is a squeeze-out transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction a squeeze-out transaction (see the question about s 2(1))?
      `the other approvals have been obtained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the approvals required by or under the Act or the articles been obtained?
      `every affected class approved it by ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has each class of shares affected approved it by ordinary resolution, voting separately?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation carry out this squeeze-out transaction` IS
    `the corporation may carry out the squeeze-out transaction within s 194` `it is a squeeze-out transaction` `the other approvals have been obtained` `every affected class approved it by ordinary resolution`

§§ `Take-over bids: being bought out, or buying out (Part XVII, ss 206 and 206.1)`

-- After a take-over bid for all the shares of a class of a distributing corporation, an offeror who has had
-- at least 90 per cent accepted may buy out the holdouts ("dissenting offerees"). A shareholder who never
-- got the offeror's notice may require the offeror to buy them out.

@export Am I a dissenting offeree (s 206(1))?
GIVEN `a take-over bid was made for all the shares of my class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a take-over bid made for all the shares of a class of shares?
      `I hold a share of that class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold a share of that class?
      `I have accepted the take-over bid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you accepted the take-over bid?
      `I acquired my share from a holder who had not accepted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you acquire your share from a holder who had not accepted the bid?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a dissenting offeree` IF
    `a person is a dissenting offeree within s 206(1)` `a take-over bid was made for all the shares of my class` `I hold a share of that class` `I have accepted the take-over bid` `I acquired my share from a holder who had not accepted`

@export Is this offer a take-over bid under the Act (s 206(1))?
GIVEN `it is made by an offeror to shareholders of a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made by an offeror to shareholders of a distributing corporation?
      `it is made at about the same time to all of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made at approximately the same time to all of them?
      `it is to acquire all the shares of a class of issued shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it to acquire all of the shares of a class of issued shares?
      `it is a distributing corporation's offer to repurchase all the shares of a class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an offer by a distributing corporation to repurchase all of the shares of a class of its shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this offer a take-over bid under the Act` IF
    `an offer is a take-over bid within s 206(1)` `it is made by an offeror to shareholders of a distributing corporation` `it is made at about the same time to all of them` `it is to acquire all the shares of a class of issued shares` `it is a distributing corporation's offer to repurchase all the shares of a class`

@export Does my interest count as a "share" in the take-over rules (s 206(1))?
GIVEN `the kind of interest` IS A `Kind of interest for the word share in s 206(1)` @desc What kind of interest is it? Choose the closest listed kind, or "an interest that is none of these".
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my interest count as a "share" in the take-over rules` IF
    `the interest is a share within s 206(1)` `the kind of interest`

@export Is this person an offeror (s 206(1))?
GIVEN `the person makes a take-over bid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person make a take-over bid?
      `the person is only an agent or mandatary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an agent or mandatary?
      `the person makes bids jointly or in concert with others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person one of two or more persons who, directly or indirectly, make take-over bids jointly or in concert?
      `the person intends to vote jointly or in concert with others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person one of two or more persons who, directly or indirectly, intend to exercise jointly or in concert voting rights attached to shares for which a bid is made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this person an offeror` IF
    `a person is an offeror within s 206(1)` `the person makes a take-over bid` `the person is only an agent or mandatary` `the person makes bids jointly or in concert with others` `the person intends to vote jointly or in concert with others`

@export Is the offeror entitled to buy out the holdouts (s 206(2))?
GIVEN `the number of shares of the class to which the bid relates` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares are there of the class to which the take-over bid relates?
      `the number held by the offeror or its affiliates or associates` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those shares were held, at the date of the bid, by or on behalf of the offeror or an affiliate or associate of the offeror?
      `the number accepted within 120 days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares were the subject of acceptances received within 120 days after the date of the bid?
      `the offeror complies with section 206` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offeror comply with section 206?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the offeror entitled to buy out the holdouts` IF
    `the offeror is entitled to acquire the shares held by the dissenting offerees within s 206(2)` (`the bid has been accepted by not less than ninety per cent within s 206(2)` `the number of shares of the class to which the bid relates` `the number held by the offeror or its affiliates or associates` `the number accepted within 120 days`) `the offeror complies with section 206`

@export By what day must an acceptance be received to count toward the 90 per cent (s 206(2))?
GIVEN `the date of the take-over bid` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the take-over bid? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must an acceptance be received to count toward the 90 per cent` IS
    `the last day for acceptances to count within s 206(2)` `the date of the take-over bid`

@export Does an acceptance received on a given day count toward the 90 per cent (s 206(2))?
GIVEN `the date of the take-over bid` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the take-over bid? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-01)
      `the day the acceptance was received` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the acceptance received? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-29)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does an acceptance received on a given day count toward the 90 per cent` IF
    `the acceptance counts within s 206(2)` `the date of the take-over bid` `the day the acceptance was received`

@export By what day must the offeror send me its notice (s 206(3))?
GIVEN `the date of termination of the take-over bid` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the take-over bid terminate? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-01)
      `the date of the take-over bid` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the take-over bid? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the offeror send me its notice` IS
    `the last day for the offeror's notice within s 206(3)` `the date of termination of the take-over bid` `the date of the take-over bid`

@export Did the offeror send me its notice in time (s 206(3))?
GIVEN `the date of termination of the take-over bid` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the take-over bid terminate? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-01)
      `the date of the take-over bid` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the take-over bid? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-01)
      `the day the offeror sent the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the offeror send the notice? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-31)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the offeror send me its notice in time` IF
    `the offeror's notice was sent in time within s 206(3)` `the date of termination of the take-over bid` `the date of the take-over bid` `the day the offeror sent the notice`

@export Does the offeror's notice say everything the Act requires (s 206(3))?
GIVEN `it says that holders of at least 90 per cent accepted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that offerees holding not less than 90 per cent of the shares accepted the bid?
      `it says the offeror is bound to take up and pay for the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the offeror is bound to take up and pay for, or has taken up and paid for, the shares of those who accepted?
      `it says I must elect to transfer or demand fair value within 20 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that a dissenting offeree is required to elect, by notifying the offeror within twenty days, to transfer the shares or to demand payment of fair value?
      `it says that silence is a deemed election to transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that a dissenting offeree who does not so notify is deemed to have elected to transfer the shares on the same terms?
      `it says I must send my shares within 20 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that a dissenting offeree must send the shares to the offeree corporation within twenty days after receiving the notice?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the offeror's notice say everything the Act requires` IF
    `the offeror's notice states what s 206(3) requires` `it says that holders of at least 90 per cent accepted` `it says the offeror is bound to take up and pay for the shares` `it says I must elect to transfer or demand fair value within 20 days` `it says that silence is a deemed election to transfer` `it says I must send my shares within 20 days`

@export Was the offeror's notice sent in the way the Act requires (s 206(3))?
GIVEN `it was sent by registered mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice sent by registered mail?
      `it was sent to every dissenting offeree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sent to each dissenting offeree?
      `it was sent to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sent to the Director?
      `it was sent in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sent within the time limits of section 206(3)?
      `it says what section 206(3) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state what section 206(3) requires?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the offeror's notice sent in the way the Act requires` IF
    `the offeror's notice complies with s 206(3)` `it was sent by registered mail` `it was sent to every dissenting offeree` `it was sent to the Director` `it was sent in time` `it says what section 206(3) requires`

@export Must the offeror send the offeree corporation a notice of adverse claim about my shares (s 206(4))?
GIVEN `the offeror sends an offeror's notice to dissenting offerees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offeror send an offeror's notice under section 206(3)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the offeror send the offeree corporation a notice of adverse claim about my shares` IF
    `the offeror must send the offeree corporation a notice of adverse claim for each share held by a dissenting offeree within s 206(4)` `the offeror sends an offeror's notice to dissenting offerees`

@export Is the offeror's notice of adverse claim in order (s 206(4))?
GIVEN `it was sent at the same time as the offeror's notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sent concurrently with the offeror's notice?
      `it follows section 78` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in accordance with section 78?
      `it covers each share a dissenting offeree holds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it cover each share held by a dissenting offeree?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the offeror's notice of adverse claim in order` IF
    `the notice of adverse claim complies with s 206(4)` `it was sent at the same time as the offeror's notice` `it follows section 78` `it covers each share a dissenting offeree holds`

@export By what day must I send my share certificates and make my election (s 206(5))?
GIVEN `the day I received the offeror's notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you receive the offeror's notice? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I send my share certificates and make my election` IS
    `the last day for the dissenting offeree to send the certificates and elect within s 206(5)` `the day I received the offeror's notice`

@export Did I send my share certificates in time (s 206(5))?
GIVEN `the day I received the offeror's notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you receive the offeror's notice? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-01)
      `the day I sent my certificates` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you send your share certificates? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-21)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I send my share certificates in time` IF
    `the certificates were sent in time within s 206(5)(a)` `the day I received the offeror's notice` `the day I sent my certificates`

@export Am I treated as having taken the bid's terms, or as demanding fair value (s 206(5))?
GIVEN `I notified the offeror that I demand fair value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you notify the offeror that you demand payment of the fair value of your shares?
      `the day I received the offeror's notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you receive the offeror's notice? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-01)
      `the day I notified the offeror` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you notify the offeror? (ISO 8601; any date if you did not)
GIVETH AN `Election of a dissenting offeree under s 206(5)`
DECIDE `Am I treated as having taken the bid's terms, or as demanding fair value` IS
    `the election of the dissenting offeree within s 206(5) and s 206(5.1)` `I notified the offeror that I demand fair value` `the day I received the offeror's notice` `the day I notified the offeror`

@export By what day must the offeror pay or transfer the consideration to the offeree corporation (s 206(6))?
GIVEN `the day the offeror sent its notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the offeror send its notice under section 206(3)? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the offeror pay or transfer the consideration to the offeree corporation` IS
    `the last day for the offeror to pay or transfer to the offeree corporation within s 206(6)` `the day the offeror sent its notice`

@export Did the offeror pay or transfer the consideration in time (s 206(6))?
GIVEN `the day the offeror sent its notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the offeror send its notice under section 206(3)? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-01)
      `the day the offeror paid or transferred` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the offeror pay or transfer it? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-21)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the offeror pay or transfer the consideration in time` IF
    `the offeror paid or transferred in time within s 206(6)` `the day the offeror sent its notice` `the day the offeror paid or transferred`

@export Does the offeree corporation hold the money for me in trust (s 206(7))?
GIVEN `the offeree corporation has received the money or consideration from the offeror` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the offeree corporation received money or other consideration under section 206(6)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the offeree corporation hold the money for me in trust` IF
    `the offeree corporation holds the money or consideration in trust for the dissenting shareholders within s 206(7)` `the offeree corporation has received the money or consideration from the offeror`

@export Has the offeree corporation kept the money safe as the Act requires (s 206(7))?
GIVEN `the money is in a separate account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the money deposited in a separate account?
      `the bank's deposits are insured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the account in a bank or other body corporate whose deposits are insured by the Canada Deposit Insurance Corporation or guaranteed by the Quebec Deposit Insurance Board?
      `other consideration is held in custody by a bank` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any other consideration placed in the custody of a bank or such other body corporate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the offeree corporation kept the money safe as the Act requires` IF
    `the deposit and custody comply with s 206(7)` `the money is in a separate account` `the bank's deposits are insured` `other consideration is held in custody by a bank`

@export Does the corporation hold the money for me in trust when it is the one making the bid (s 206(7.1))?
GIVEN `the corporation is making a bid to repurchase all the shares of a class of its shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation an offeror making a take-over bid to repurchase all the shares of a class of its own shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the corporation hold the money for me in trust when it is the one making the bid` IF
    `the corporation holds the money and consideration in trust for the dissenting shareholders within s 206(7.1)` `the corporation is making a bid to repurchase all the shares of a class of its shares`

@export By what day must the corporation deposit the money when it is the one making the bid (s 206(7.1))?
GIVEN `the day a notice was sent under section 206(3)` IS A DATE @desc On what day was a notice sent under section 206(3)? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the corporation deposit the money when it is the one making the bid` IS
    `the last day for the corporation to deposit the money within s 206(7.1)` `the day a notice was sent under section 206(3)`

@export Did the corporation deposit the money in time when it is the one making the bid (s 206(7.1))?
GIVEN `the day a notice was sent under section 206(3)` IS A DATE @desc On what day was a notice sent under section 206(3)? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-01)
      `the day the corporation deposited the money` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the corporation deposit the money? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-21)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the corporation deposit the money in time when it is the one making the bid` IF
    `the corporation deposited in time within s 206(7.1)` `the day a notice was sent under section 206(3)` `the day the corporation deposited the money`

@export By what day must the offeree corporation act on the offeror's payment (s 206(8))?
GIVEN `the day the offeror sent its notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the offeror send its notice under section 206(3)? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the offeree corporation act on the offeror's payment` IS
    `the last day for the offeree corporation to act within s 206(8)` `the day the offeror sent its notice`

@export Did the offeree corporation act in time (s 206(8))?
GIVEN `the day the offeror sent its notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the offeror send its notice under section 206(3)? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-01)
      `the day the offeree corporation acted` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the offeree corporation act? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-31)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the offeree corporation act in time` IF
    `the offeree corporation acted in time within s 206(8)` `the day the offeror sent its notice` `the day the offeree corporation acted`

@export Must the offeree corporation issue the offeror a share certificate for my shares (s 206(8)(a))?
GIVEN `the offeror has paid or transferred what s 206(6) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the payment or transfer required by section 206(6) been made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the offeree corporation issue the offeror a share certificate for my shares` IF
    `the offeree corporation must issue the offeror a share certificate within s 206(8)(a)` `the offeror has paid or transferred what s 206(6) requires`

@export Must the offeree corporation give me the money or consideration for my shares (s 206(8)(b))?
GIVEN `I elected to accept the bid's terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you elect to accept the take-over bid terms?
      `I sent my certificates as section 206(5)(a) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you send your share certificates as section 206(5)(a) requires?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the offeree corporation give me the money or consideration for my shares` IF
    `the offeree corporation must give the dissenting offeree the money or consideration within s 206(8)(b)` `I elected to accept the bid's terms` `I sent my certificates as section 206(5)(a) requires`

@export Must the offeree corporation send me a notice that my shares were cancelled and the money is held for me (s 206(8)(c))?
GIVEN `the offeror has paid or transferred what s 206(6) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the payment or transfer required by section 206(6) been made?
      `the money is deposited as section 206(7) or 206(7.1) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the money or other consideration deposited as section 206(7) or 206(7.1) requires?
      `I have not sent my certificates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you not sent your share certificates as section 206(5)(a) requires?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the offeree corporation send me a notice that my shares were cancelled and the money is held for me` IF
    `the offeree corporation must send the dissenting shareholder the notice within s 206(8)(c)` `the offeror has paid or transferred what s 206(6) requires` `the money is deposited as section 206(7) or 206(7.1) requires` `I have not sent my certificates`

@export Does the offeree corporation's notice to me say what the Act requires (s 206(8)(c))?
GIVEN `it says my shares have been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that your shares have been cancelled?
      `it says the money is held in trust for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the offeree corporation or a designated person holds in trust the money or consideration to which you are entitled?
      `it says it will send the money after receiving my shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the offeree corporation will, subject to subsections 206(9) to 206(18), send that money or consideration to you without delay after receiving the shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the offeree corporation's notice to me say what the Act requires` IF
    `the offeree corporation's notice states what s 206(8)(c) requires` `it says my shares have been cancelled` `it says the money is held in trust for me` `it says it will send the money after receiving my shares`

@export May the offeror ask a court to fix the fair value of my shares (s 206(9))?
GIVEN `I elected to demand fair value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you elect to demand payment of the fair value of your shares?
      `the day the offeror paid or transferred` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the offeror pay or transfer under section 206(6)? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-21)
      `the day the offeror applied to the court` IS A DATE @desc On what day did (or will) the offeror apply to the court? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-08-10)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the offeror ask a court to fix the fair value of my shares` IF
    `the offeror may apply to a court to fix the fair value within s 206(9)` `I elected to demand fair value` `the day the offeror paid or transferred` `the day the offeror applied to the court`

@export By what day may the offeror ask a court to fix the fair value (s 206(9))?
GIVEN `the day the offeror paid or transferred` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the offeror pay or transfer under section 206(6)? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-21)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day may the offeror ask a court to fix the fair value` IS
    `the last day for the offeror to apply to a court within s 206(9)` `the day the offeror paid or transferred`

@export May I ask a court to fix the fair value of my shares myself (s 206(10))?
GIVEN `the offeror did not apply to a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the offeror fail to apply to a court under section 206(9)?
      `the day the offeror paid or transferred` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the offeror pay or transfer under section 206(6)? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-21)
      `the day I apply to the court` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you apply (or did you apply) to the court? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-08-20)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask a court to fix the fair value of my shares myself` IF
    `the dissenting offeree may apply to a court to fix the fair value within s 206(10)` `the offeror did not apply to a court` `the day the offeror paid or transferred` `the day I apply to the court`

@export By what day may I ask a court to fix the fair value of my shares (s 206(10))?
GIVEN `the day the offeror paid or transferred` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the offeror pay or transfer under section 206(6)? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-21)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day may I ask a court to fix the fair value of my shares` IS
    `the last day for the dissenting offeree to apply to a court within s 206(10)` `the day the offeror paid or transferred`

@export Am I treated as having taken the bid's terms because no one applied to a court (s 206(11))?
GIVEN `no application was made to a court under section 206(10) in the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was no application made to a court under section 206(10) within the period it sets?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Election of a dissenting offeree under s 206(5)`
DECIDE `Am I treated as having taken the bid's terms because no one applied to a court` IS
    `the deemed election within s 206(11)` `no application was made to a court under section 206(10) in the period`

@export Is this the right court to apply to about take-over shares (s 206(12))?
GIVEN `it has jurisdiction where the corporation has its registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court have jurisdiction in the place where the corporation has its registered office?
      `it has jurisdiction in the province where I live` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court have jurisdiction in the province where the dissenting offeree resides?
      `the corporation carries on business in my province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation carry on business in that province?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this the right court to apply to about take-over shares` IF
    `the court is a proper court within s 206(12)` `it has jurisdiction where the corporation has its registered office` `it has jurisdiction in the province where I live` `the corporation carries on business in my province`

@export Must I give security for costs when I apply to the court about take-over shares (s 206(13))?
GIVEN `the application is under section 206(9) or 206(10)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made under section 206(9) or 206(10)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give security for costs when I apply to the court about take-over shares` IS
    `a dissenting offeree is required to give security for costs within s 206(13)` `the application is under section 206(9) or 206(10)`

@export Will I be a party to the court application about take-over shares and bound by its decision (s 206(14))?
GIVEN `I elected to demand fair value and the offeror has not acquired my shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you elect under section 206(5)(b)(ii) to demand payment of fair value, and has the offeror not acquired your shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will I be a party to the court application about take-over shares and bound by its decision` IF
    `the dissenting offeree must be joined as a party and is bound by the decision within s 206(14)(a)` `I elected to demand fair value and the offeror has not acquired my shares`

@export Has the offeror told me what it must about the court application (s 206(14))?
GIVEN `the notice states the date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offeror's notice state the date of the application?
      `the notice states the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the place of the application?
      `the notice states the consequences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the consequences of the application?
      `the notice states my right to appear and be heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state your right to appear and be heard in person or by counsel?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the offeror told me what it must about the court application` IF
    `the offeror's notice to the dissenting offeree complies with s 206(14)(b)` `the notice states the date` `the notice states the place` `the notice states the consequences` `the notice states my right to appear and be heard`

@export Will the court fix a fair value for the shares of all dissenting offerees together (s 206(15))?
GIVEN `an application has been made to a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made to a court under section 206(9) or 206(10)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the court fix a fair value for the shares of all dissenting offerees together` IF
    `the court must fix a fair value for the shares of all dissenting offerees within s 206(15)` `an application has been made to a court`

@export May the court appoint appraisers to help fix the fair value of my shares (s 206(16))?
GIVEN `an application has been made to a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made to a court under section 206(9) or 206(10)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court appoint appraisers to help fix the fair value of my shares` IF
    `the court may appoint appraisers within s 206(16)` `an application has been made to a court`

@export Will the court's final order be against the offeror and in my favour (s 206(17))?
GIVEN `the court has fixed a fair value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court fixed a fair value for the shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the court's final order be against the offeror and in my favour` IF
    `the final order is made against the offeror in favour of each dissenting offeree within s 206(17)` `the court has fixed a fair value`

@export May the court make this order in the proceedings about my shares (s 206(18))?
GIVEN `the court thinks the order fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court think the order fit?
      `it is made in proceedings under section 206` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order made in connection with proceedings under section 206?
      `the order` IS A `Kind of order under s 206(18)` @desc What order is sought? Choose the closest listed kind, or "any other order the court thinks fit under s 206(18)".
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court make this order in the proceedings about my shares` IF
    `the court may make the order within s 206(18)` `the court thinks the order fit` `it is made in proceedings under section 206` `the order`

@export May the court allow interest on what I am owed for my take-over shares for the day I am asking about (s 206(18))?
GIVEN `the day I sent or delivered my certificates` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you send or deliver your share certificates under section 206(5)? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-21)
      `the day of payment` IS A DATE @desc On what day was (or will) the payment be made? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-08-31)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-08-15)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court allow interest on what I am owed for my take-over shares for the day I am asking about` IF
    `the court may allow interest for a day within s 206(18)(c)` `the day I sent or delivered my certificates` `the day of payment` `the day I am asking about`

@export By what day may I require the offeror to buy my shares, because I never got its notice (s 206.1(1))?
GIVEN `I received an offer under the take-over bid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive an offer pursuant to the take-over bid?
      `the date of termination of the take-over bid` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the take-over bid terminate? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-01)
      `the day I learned of the take-over bid` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you learn of the take-over bid? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-20)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day may I require the offeror to buy my shares, because I never got its notice` IS
    `the last day for the shareholder to require the offeror to acquire within s 206.1(1)` (`the day the ninety days for the shareholder start within s 206.1(1)` `I received an offer under the take-over bid` `the date of termination of the take-over bid` `the day I learned of the take-over bid`)

@export May I require the offeror to buy my shares, because I never got its notice (s 206.1(1))?
GIVEN `I hold shares of a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold shares of a distributing corporation?
      `I did not receive an offeror's notice under section 206(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not receive an offeror's notice under section 206(3)?
      `I received an offer under the take-over bid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive an offer pursuant to the take-over bid?
      `the date of termination of the take-over bid` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the take-over bid terminate? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-01)
      `the day I learned of the take-over bid` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you learn of the take-over bid? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-20)
      `the day I required the offeror to acquire my shares` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you (or will you) require the offeror to acquire your shares? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-08-30)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I require the offeror to buy my shares, because I never got its notice` IF
    `the shareholder may require the offeror to acquire the shares within s 206.1(1)` `I hold shares of a distributing corporation` `I did not receive an offeror's notice under section 206(3)` (`the day the ninety days for the shareholder start within s 206.1(1)` `I received an offer under the take-over bid` `the date of termination of the take-over bid` `the day I learned of the take-over bid`) `the day I required the offeror to acquire my shares`

@export Must the offeror buy my shares on the same terms as those who accepted (s 206.1(2))?
GIVEN `I have required the offeror to acquire my shares under section 206.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you required the offeror to acquire your shares under section 206.1(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the offeror buy my shares on the same terms as those who accepted` IF
    `the offeror must acquire the shares on the same terms as the offerees who accepted within s 206.1(2)` `I have required the offeror to acquire my shares under section 206.1(1)`

§§ `Winding up and reviving a corporation (Part XVIII, ss 207 to 213)`

-- A corporation ends in one of four ways: its directors or shareholders dissolve it (ss 210, 211), the
-- Director dissolves it (s 212), or a court does (ss 213, 214). A dissolved body corporate can be revived (s 209).
-- Ss 214 to 220 (court-ordered liquidation) and 221 to 228 (the liquidator, and what follows dissolution) are below.

@export Is this the right court for a dissolution application (s 207)?
GIVEN `the court has jurisdiction where the corporation has its registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court have jurisdiction in the place where the corporation has its registered office?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this the right court for a dissolution application` IF
    `a court is the court of this Part within s 207` `the court has jurisdiction where the corporation has its registered office`

@export Do the dissolution rules apply to my corporation if it is insolvent or bankrupt (s 208(1))?
GIVEN `the provision is section 209 or section 212` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision you are asking about section 209 (revival) or section 212 (dissolution by the Director)?
      `the corporation is an insolvent person as defined in the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation an insolvent person as defined in the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act?
      `the corporation is a bankrupt as defined in the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a bankrupt as defined in the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the dissolution rules apply to my corporation if it is insolvent or bankrupt` IF
    `this Part applies to the corporation within s 208(1)` `the provision is section 209 or section 212` `the corporation is an insolvent person as defined in the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act` `the corporation is a bankrupt as defined in the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act`

@export Are the proceedings to dissolve my corporation stayed (s 208(2))?
GIVEN `proceedings are taken under this Part to dissolve or to liquidate and dissolve the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are proceedings being taken under the Act to dissolve, or to liquidate and dissolve, the corporation?
      `the corporation is found in a proceeding under the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act to be an insolvent person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation been found, in a proceeding under the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act, to be an insolvent person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the proceedings to dissolve my corporation stayed` IF
    `the proceedings are stayed within s 208(2)` `proceedings are taken under this Part to dissolve or to liquidate and dissolve the corporation` `the corporation is found in a proceeding under the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act to be an insolvent person`

@export Can I apply to the Director to revive a dissolved body corporate (s 209(1))?
GIVEN `the way the body corporate was dissolved` IS A `Way a body corporate was dissolved for s 209(1)` @desc How was the body corporate dissolved? Choose the closest listed way, or "dissolved in some other way".
      `I am an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an interested person (see the question about s 209(6))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I apply to the Director to revive a dissolved body corporate` IF
    `an interested person may apply to the Director for revival within s 209(1)` `the way the body corporate was dissolved` `I am an interested person`

@export Must the Director issue me a certificate of revival (s 209(3))?
GIVEN `the Director has received articles of revival` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director received articles of revival?
      `the dissolved body corporate has fulfilled all conditions precedent that the Director considers reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the dissolved body corporate fulfilled all the conditions precedent that the Director considers reasonable?
      `there is a valid reason for refusing to issue the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a valid reason for refusing to issue the certificate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director issue me a certificate of revival` IF
    `the Director must issue a certificate of revival within s 209(3)` `the Director has received articles of revival` `the dissolved body corporate has fulfilled all conditions precedent that the Director considers reasonable` `there is a valid reason for refusing to issue the certificate`

@export Is the body corporate revived as a corporation on a given day (s 209(3.1))?
GIVEN `the date shown on the certificate of revival` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown on the certificate of revival? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-11-01)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know whether it is revived? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-11-15)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the body corporate revived as a corporation on a given day` IF
    `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under this Act on a day within s 209(3.1)` `the date shown on the certificate of revival` `the day asked about`

@export Is the revived corporation put back as it was in respect of a matter (s 209(4))?
GIVEN `the body corporate has been revived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the body corporate been revived?
      `the matter` IS A `Matter that limits the restoration under s 209(4)` @desc Which matter is in play? Choose "none of these" if it is none of the listed ones.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the revived corporation put back as it was in respect of a matter` IF
    `the revived corporation is restored to its previous position in respect of the matter within s 209(4)(a)` `the body corporate has been revived` `the matter`

@export Is a legal action taken between dissolution and revival valid (s 209(5))?
GIVEN `the body corporate has been revived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the body corporate been revived?
      `the legal action respecting its affairs was taken between its dissolution and its revival` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the legal action respecting its affairs taken between its dissolution and its revival?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a legal action taken between dissolution and revival valid` IF
    `a legal action taken between dissolution and revival is valid and effective within s 209(5)` `the body corporate has been revived` `the legal action respecting its affairs was taken between its dissolution and its revival`

@export Am I an "interested person" who can ask for revival (s 209(6))?
GIVEN `what I am to the dissolved body corporate` IS A `Kind of person named in s 209(6)` @desc What are you to the dissolved body corporate? Choose the closest listed kind, or "a person not named in s 209(6)".
      `the contract is, in Quebec, a contract by gratuitous title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your connection is a contract: is it, in Quebec, a contract by gratuitous title?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an "interested person" who can ask for revival` IS
    `whether the person is an interested person within s 209(6)` `what I am to the dissolved body corporate` `the contract is, in Quebec, a contract by gratuitous title`

@export Can the directors alone dissolve a corporation that has never issued shares (s 210(1))?
GIVEN `the corporation has issued shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation issued any shares?
      `all the directors have resolved to dissolve it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all the directors resolved to dissolve it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the directors alone dissolve a corporation that has never issued shares` IF
    `the corporation may be dissolved by resolution of all the directors within s 210(1)` `the corporation has issued shares` `all the directors have resolved to dissolve it`

@export Can the shareholders dissolve a corporation that has no property and no liabilities (s 210(2))?
GIVEN `the corporation has no property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have no property?
      `the corporation has no liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have no liabilities?
      `the corporation has issued more than one class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation issued more than one class of shares?
      `the number of votes cast in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast in favour of the resolution at the meeting?
      `the number of votes cast against` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast against the resolution at the meeting?
      `the resolution was signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on it?
      `every class has approved by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is more than one class: did the holders of each class approve by special resolution, whether or not otherwise entitled to vote?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the shareholders dissolve a corporation that has no property and no liabilities` IF
    `the corporation may be dissolved by special resolution within s 210(2)` `the corporation has no property` `the corporation has no liabilities` `the corporation has issued more than one class of shares` (`Vote tally` WITH `votes cast in favour` IS `the number of votes cast in favour`, `votes cast against` IS `the number of votes cast against`, `signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on the resolution` IS `the resolution was signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote`) `every class has approved by special resolution`

@export Can the shareholders dissolve a corporation that still has property or liabilities (s 210(3))?
GIVEN `the corporation has property or liabilities or both` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have property, or liabilities, or both?
      `the corporation has issued more than one class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation issued more than one class of shares?
      `the number of votes cast in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast in favour of the resolution at the meeting?
      `the number of votes cast against` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast against the resolution at the meeting?
      `the resolution was signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on it?
      `every class has approved by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is more than one class: did the holders of each class approve by special resolution, whether or not otherwise entitled to vote?
      `the resolutions authorize the directors to cause the corporation to distribute any property and discharge any liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the resolutions authorize the directors to cause the corporation to distribute any property and discharge any liabilities?
      `the corporation distributed its property and discharged its liabilities before sending articles of dissolution to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation distribute its property and discharge its liabilities before sending the articles of dissolution to the Director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the shareholders dissolve a corporation that still has property or liabilities` IF
    `the corporation may be dissolved by special resolution within s 210(3)` `the corporation has property or liabilities or both` `the corporation has issued more than one class of shares` (`Vote tally` WITH `votes cast in favour` IS `the number of votes cast in favour`, `votes cast against` IS `the number of votes cast against`, `signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on the resolution` IS `the resolution was signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote`) `every class has approved by special resolution` `the resolutions authorize the directors to cause the corporation to distribute any property and discharge any liabilities` `the corporation distributed its property and discharged its liabilities before sending articles of dissolution to the Director`

@export Does the corporation still exist on a given day after articles of dissolution (s 210(6))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of dissolution` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of dissolution? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-12-01)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know whether it exists? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-11-30)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the corporation still exist on a given day after articles of dissolution` IF
    `the corporation exists on a day within s 210(6)` `the date shown in the certificate of dissolution` `the day asked about`

@export May I propose a voluntary liquidation and dissolution (s 211(1))?
GIVEN `I am a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director?
      `I am a shareholder entitled to vote at an annual meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shareholder entitled to vote at an annual meeting of shareholders?
      `my proposal is made in accordance with section 137` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your proposal made in accordance with section 137 (shareholder proposals)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I propose a voluntary liquidation and dissolution` IF
    `a person may propose voluntary liquidation and dissolution within s 211(1)` `I am a director` `I am a shareholder entitled to vote at an annual meeting of shareholders` `my proposal is made in accordance with section 137`

@export Can the corporation liquidate and dissolve voluntarily (s 211(3))?
GIVEN `the corporation has issued more than one class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation issued more than one class of shares?
      `the number of votes cast in favour` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast in favour of the resolution at the meeting?
      `the number of votes cast against` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast against the resolution at the meeting?
      `the resolution was signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on it?
      `every class has approved by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is more than one class: did the holders of each class approve by special resolution, whether or not otherwise entitled to vote?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the corporation liquidate and dissolve voluntarily` IF
    `the corporation may liquidate and dissolve within s 211(3)` `the corporation has issued more than one class of shares` (`Vote tally` WITH `votes cast in favour` IS `the number of votes cast in favour`, `votes cast against` IS `the number of votes cast against`, `signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on the resolution` IS `the resolution was signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote`) `every class has approved by special resolution`

@export May the corporation keep carrying on business after the certificate of intent to dissolve (s 211(6))?
GIVEN `a certificate of intent to dissolve has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a certificate of intent to dissolve been issued?
      `the business is necessary for the liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business necessary for the liquidation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation keep carrying on business after the certificate of intent to dissolve` IF
    `the corporation may carry on the business within s 211(6)` `a certificate of intent to dissolve has been issued` `the business is necessary for the liquidation`

@export Must the corporation notify each known creditor straight away (s 211(7)(a))?
GIVEN `a certificate of intent to dissolve has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a certificate of intent to dissolve been issued?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation notify each known creditor straight away` IF
    `the corporation must immediately notify each known creditor within s 211(7)(a)` `a certificate of intent to dissolve has been issued`

@export May the corporation distribute its remaining property among its shareholders (s 211(7)(d))?
GIVEN `the corporation has given the notices required by paragraphs 211(7)(a) and 211(7)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation given the notices that paragraphs 211(7)(a) and (b) require?
      `the corporation has adequately provided for the payment or discharge of all its obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation adequately provided for the payment or discharge of all its obligations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation distribute its remaining property among its shareholders` IF
    `the corporation shall distribute its remaining property among its shareholders within s 211(7)(d)` `the corporation has given the notices required by paragraphs 211(7)(a) and 211(7)(b)` `the corporation has adequately provided for the payment or discharge of all its obligations`

@export Can I ask a court to supervise the liquidation (s 211(8))?
GIVEN `I am the Director or an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Director or an interested person?
      `the application is made during the liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made during the liquidation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I ask a court to supervise the liquidation` IF
    `the Director or an interested person may apply for the court's supervision within s 211(8)` `I am the Director or an interested person` `the application is made during the liquidation`

@export Must I give the Director notice of my application to a court about the liquidation (s 211(9))?
GIVEN `I have applied under section 211` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied to a court under section 211?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give the Director notice of my application to a court about the liquidation` IF
    `the applicant must give the Director notice of the application within s 211(9)` `I have applied under section 211`

@export Can the certificate of intent to dissolve be revoked (s 211(10))?
GIVEN `a certificate of intent to dissolve has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a certificate of intent to dissolve been issued?
      `a certificate of dissolution has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a certificate of dissolution been issued?
      `the statement of revocation is in the form the Director fixes and has been sent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a statement of revocation, in the form the Director fixes, been sent to the Director?
      `the revocation is approved in the same manner as the resolution under subsection 211(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the revocation been approved in the same manner as the resolution to liquidate and dissolve?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the certificate of intent to dissolve be revoked` IF
    `the certificate of intent to dissolve may be revoked within s 211(10)` `a certificate of intent to dissolve has been issued` `a certificate of dissolution has been issued` `the statement of revocation is in the form the Director fixes and has been sent` `the revocation is approved in the same manner as the resolution under subsection 211(3)`

@export From what day may the corporation carry on business again after a revocation (s 211(12))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of revocation of intent to dissolve` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of revocation of intent to dissolve? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-12-01)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-12-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `From what day may the corporation carry on business again after a revocation` IF
    `the revocation is effective and the corporation may continue its business on a day within s 211(12)` `the date shown in the certificate of revocation of intent to dissolve` `the day asked about`

@export Must the corporation now prepare articles of dissolution (s 211(13))?
GIVEN `the certificate of intent to dissolve has not been revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the certificate of intent to dissolve not been revoked?
      `the corporation has complied with subsection 211(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation complied with subsection 211(7)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation now prepare articles of dissolution` IF
    `the corporation shall prepare articles of dissolution within s 211(13)` `the certificate of intent to dissolve has not been revoked` `the corporation has complied with subsection 211(7)`

@export Does the corporation still exist on a given day after a voluntary liquidation (s 211(16))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of dissolution` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of dissolution? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2027-01-01)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know whether it exists? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-12-31)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the corporation still exist on a given day after a voluntary liquidation` IF
    `the corporation exists on a day within s 211(16)` `the date shown in the certificate of dissolution` `the day asked about`

@export Has the corporation not started business within three years of its certificate of incorporation (s 212(1)(a)(i))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of incorporation` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of incorporation? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2023-01-01)
      `the corporation has commenced business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation commenced business?
      `the day the corporation commenced business` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day did it commence business? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2023-06-01; any date if it has not)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-01-02)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation not started business within three years of its certificate of incorporation` IF
    `the corporation has not commenced business within three years after the date shown in its certificate of incorporation on a day within s 212(1)(a)(i)` `the date shown in the certificate of incorporation` `the corporation has commenced business` `the day the corporation commenced business` `the day asked about`

@export Has the corporation failed to carry on its business for three consecutive years (s 212(1)(a)(ii))?
GIVEN `the number of consecutive years the corporation has not carried on its business` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many consecutive years has the corporation not carried on its business?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation failed to carry on its business for three consecutive years` IF
    `the corporation has not carried on its business for three consecutive years within s 212(1)(a)(ii)` `the number of consecutive years the corporation has not carried on its business`

@export Has the corporation been in default for a year in sending the Director a fee, notice or document (s 212(1)(a)(iii))?
GIVEN `the day the default began` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the default begin? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2025-01-01)
      `the default is continuing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the default continuing?
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-01-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation been in default for a year in sending the Director a fee, notice or document` IF
    `the corporation is in default for one year in sending a fee, notice, document or information within s 212(1)(a)(iii)` `the day the default began` `the default is continuing` `the day asked about`

@export Does the corporation have no directors (s 212(1)(a)(iv))?
GIVEN `the corporation does not have any directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have no directors at all?
      `the corporation is in the situation described in subsection 109(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation in the situation described in subsection 109(4)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the corporation have no directors` IF
    `the corporation has no directors or is in the situation of s 109(4) within s 212(1)(a)(iv)` `the corporation does not have any directors` `the corporation is in the situation described in subsection 109(4)`

@export Has the Minister told the Director that my corporation is a listed entity (s 212(1)(a)(v))?
GIVEN `the Director is notified by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness that the corporation is a listed entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness notified the Director that the corporation is a listed entity (Criminal Code, s 83.01(1))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the Minister told the Director that my corporation is a listed entity` IF
    `the corporation is a listed entity notified to the Director within s 212(1)(a)(v)` `the Director is notified by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness that the corporation is a listed entity`

@export Has the Director given the notice that must come before dissolving my corporation (s 212(2))?
GIVEN `the Director gave one hundred and twenty days notice of the decision to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Director give the corporation 120 days notice of the decision to dissolve?
      `the Director gave that notice to each director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Director give that notice to each director?
      `the Director published notice of the decision in a publication generally available to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Director publish notice of the decision in a publication generally available to the public?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the Director given the notice that must come before dissolving my corporation` IF
    `the Director has met the conditions of s 212(2)` `the Director gave one hundred and twenty days notice of the decision to the corporation` `the Director gave that notice to each director` `the Director published notice of the decision in a publication generally available to the public`

@export Does the 120 days notice apply to my corporation (s 212(2.1))?
GIVEN `one of the grounds is the ground in subparagraph 212(1)(a)(v)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is one of the grounds that the corporation is a listed entity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the 120 days notice apply to my corporation` IF
    `subsection 212(2) applies within s 212(2.1)` `one of the grounds is the ground in subparagraph 212(1)(a)(v)`

@export What is the first day the Director may issue the certificate of dissolution after the notice (s 212(3))?
GIVEN `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the 120 days notice given? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the first day the Director may issue the certificate of dissolution after the notice` IS
    `the earliest day the certificate of dissolution may be issued within s 212(3)` `the day the notice was given`

@export May the Director issue a certificate of dissolution on a given day (s 212(3))?
GIVEN `cause to the contrary has been shown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has cause to the contrary been shown?
      `a court has made an order under section 246` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court made an order under section 246?
      `subsection 212(2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the 120 days notice requirement apply (it does not for a listed entity)?
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the 120 days notice given? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-01)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the certificate be issued? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-30)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Director issue a certificate of dissolution on a given day` IF
    `the Director may issue a certificate of dissolution on a day within s 212(3)` `cause to the contrary has been shown` `a court has made an order under section 246` `subsection 212(2) applies` `the day the notice was given` `the day I am asking about`

@export Can the Director dissolve my corporation because the incorporation fee was not paid (s 212(3.1))?
GIVEN `the required fee for the issuance of a certificate of incorporation has not been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the required fee for the certificate of incorporation not been paid?
      `the corporation has not complied with subsection 21.21(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation not complied with subsection 21.21(2)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Director dissolve my corporation because the incorporation fee was not paid` IF
    `the Director may dissolve the corporation despite the rest of s 212 within s 212(3.1)` `the required fee for the issuance of a certificate of incorporation has not been paid` `the corporation has not complied with subsection 21.21(2)`

@export Does the corporation still exist on a given day after the Director dissolves it (s 212(4))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of dissolution` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of dissolution? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-01)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know whether it exists? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-30)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the corporation still exist on a given day after the Director dissolves it` IF
    `the corporation exists on a day within s 212(4)` `the date shown in the certificate of dissolution` `the day asked about`

@export Can I ask a court to dissolve the corporation (s 213(1))?
GIVEN `I am the Director or an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Director or an interested person?
      `the number of consecutive years the corporation has failed to comply with the requirements about annual meetings` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many consecutive years has the corporation failed to hold annual meetings of shareholders as the Act requires?
      `the corporation has contravened subsection 16(2) or section 21, 157 or 159` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation contravened subsection 16(2) or section 21, 157 or 159?
      `the corporation has procured a certificate under this Act by misrepresentation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation procured a certificate under the Act by misrepresentation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I ask a court to dissolve the corporation` IF
    `the Director or an interested person may apply to a court for an order dissolving the corporation within s 213(1)` `I am the Director or an interested person` `the number of consecutive years the corporation has failed to comply with the requirements about annual meetings` `the corporation has contravened subsection 16(2) or section 21, 157 or 159` `the corporation has procured a certificate under this Act by misrepresentation`

@export What must the Director do when it receives a court's order about my corporation (s 213(4))?
GIVEN `the kind of order` IS A `Kind of order the Director receives under s 213(4)` @desc What kind of order did the court make?
GIVETH A `What the Director must do on receiving an order under s 213(4)`
DECIDE `What must the Director do when it receives a court's order about my corporation` IS
    `what the Director must do on receiving an order within s 213(4)` `the kind of order`

§§ `Liquidation and dissolution ordered by a court (Part XVIII, ss 214 to 220)`

-- A shareholder who is oppressed, or who has a unanimous shareholder agreement right, or who can show that
-- it is just and equitable, may ask a court to liquidate and dissolve the corporation. A liquidator is then
-- appointed and takes over the directors' and shareholders' powers.

@export Can I, as a shareholder, ask a court to liquidate and dissolve the corporation (s 214(1))?
GIVEN `I am a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shareholder of the corporation?
      `an act or omission has an oppressive result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an act or omission of the corporation or an affiliate effect a result that is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to, or that unfairly disregards, the interests of a security holder, creditor, director or officer?
      `the business or affairs are carried on in an oppressive manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the business or affairs of the corporation or an affiliate, or have they been, carried on in a manner that is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to, or that unfairly disregards, the interests of a security holder, creditor, director or officer?
      `the directors' powers are exercised in an oppressive manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the powers of the directors of the corporation or an affiliate, or have they been, exercised in a manner that is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to, or that unfairly disregards, the interests of a security holder, creditor, director or officer?
      `a unanimous shareholder agreement entitles me to demand dissolution after a specified event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a unanimous shareholder agreement entitle you, as a complaining shareholder, to demand dissolution of the corporation after the occurrence of a specified event?
      `that event has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that event occurred?
      `it is just and equitable that the corporation should be liquidated and dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it just and equitable that the corporation should be liquidated and dissolved?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I, as a shareholder, ask a court to liquidate and dissolve the corporation` IF
    `a court may order the liquidation and dissolution of the corporation or an affiliate within s 214(1)` `I am a shareholder` (`the court is satisfied of oppression within s 214(1)(a)` `an act or omission has an oppressive result` `the business or affairs are carried on in an oppressive manner` `the directors' powers are exercised in an oppressive manner`) (`the court is satisfied of a ground within s 214(1)(b)` `a unanimous shareholder agreement entitles me to demand dissolution after a specified event` `that event has occurred` `it is just and equitable that the corporation should be liquidated and dissolved`)

@export Does my application to a court for liquidation say what the Act requires (s 216(1))?
GIVEN `my application states the reasons why the corporation should be liquidated and dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your application state the reasons why the corporation should be liquidated and dissolved?
      `the reasons are verified by an affidavit of the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the reasons verified by an affidavit of the applicant?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my application to a court for liquidation say what the Act requires` IF
    `the application under s 214(1) complies with s 216(1)` `my application states the reasons why the corporation should be liquidated and dissolved` `the reasons are verified by an affidavit of the applicant`

@export By what day must the time to show cause fall (s 216(2))?
GIVEN `the date of the order` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the court's order? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the time to show cause fall` IS
    `the last day for the show cause time within s 216(2)` `the date of the order`

@export Is the time set for showing cause within four weeks of the order (s 216(2))?
GIVEN `the date of the order` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the court's order? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-01)
      `the time specified in the order for showing cause` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the order say cause is to be shown? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-29)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the time set for showing cause within four weeks of the order` IF
    `the time specified for showing cause is within four weeks after the order within s 216(2)` `the date of the order` `the time specified in the order for showing cause`

@export Can the court make the directors and officers hand over information about the corporation (s 216(3))?
GIVEN `the information is of a kind named in paragraph 216(3)(a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it financial statements, the name and address of each shareholder, or the name and address of each known creditor or claimant (including contingent claimants and those with a contract)?
      `the information is material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information material?
      `it is known to or reasonably ascertainable by the directors and officers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it known to, or reasonably ascertainable by, the directors and officers?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the court make the directors and officers hand over information about the corporation` IF
    `the information is within the order the court may make within s 216(3)` `the information is of a kind named in paragraph 216(3)(a), (b) or (c)` `the information is material` `it is known to or reasonably ascertainable by the directors and officers`

@export Has the court's show-cause order been published and served as the Act requires (s 216(4))?
GIVEN `a copy of the order was published as directed in the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a copy of the order published as directed in the order?
      `it was published at least once in each week before the time appointed for the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it published at least once in each week before the time appointed for the hearing?
      `it was published in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it published in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office?
      `a copy was served on the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a copy served on the Director?
      `a copy was served on each person named in the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a copy served on each person named in the order?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the court's show-cause order been published and served as the Act requires` IF
    `the order under s 216(2) has been published and served as s 216(4) requires` `a copy of the order was published as directed in the order` `it was published at least once in each week before the time appointed for the hearing` `it was published in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office` `a copy was served on the Director` `a copy was served on each person named in the order`

@export May the court make a given kind of order in the winding up (s 217)?
GIVEN `the kind of order` IS A `Kind of order under s 217` @desc What kind of order is being asked for? Choose the closest listed kind, or "any other order the court thinks fit under s 217".
      `the order is made in connection with the dissolution or the liquidation and dissolution of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order made in connection with the dissolution, or the liquidation and dissolution, of the corporation?
      `the court is satisfied that the corporation is able to pay or adequately provide for the discharge of all its obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the corporation is able to pay, or adequately provide for the discharge of, all its obligations?
      `the applicant is a creditor, the inspectors or the liquidator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant a creditor, the inspectors or the liquidator?
      `notice has been given to all interested parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has notice been given to all interested parties?
      `section 223 permits the distribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 223 permit the distribution?
      `the applicant is a director, officer, security holder, creditor or the liquidator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant a director, officer, security holder, creditor or the liquidator?
      `the liquidator has rendered a final account to the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the liquidator rendered a final account to the court?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court make a given kind of order in the winding up` IF
    `the court may make this kind of order within s 217` `the kind of order` (`the court may make an order under the opening words of s 217` `the order is made in connection with the dissolution or the liquidation and dissolution of the corporation` `the court is satisfied that the corporation is able to pay or adequately provide for the discharge of all its obligations`) `the applicant is a creditor, the inspectors or the liquidator` `notice has been given to all interested parties` `section 223 permits the distribution` `the applicant is a director, officer, security holder, creditor or the liquidator` `the liquidator has rendered a final account to the court`

@export Has the liquidation begun on a given day (s 218)?
GIVEN `the date the court makes the order for liquidation` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the court make the order for liquidation? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-01)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know whether it has begun? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the liquidation begun on a given day` IF
    `the liquidation has commenced on a day within s 218` `the date the court makes the order for liquidation` `the day asked about`

@export May the corporation carry on business once a liquidation order is made (s 219(1))?
GIVEN `a court has made an order for liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court made an order for liquidation?
      `the business is, in the opinion of the liquidator, required for an orderly liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business, in the liquidator's opinion, required for an orderly liquidation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation carry on business once a liquidation order is made` IF
    `the corporation may carry on the business within s 219(1)(a)` `a court has made an order for liquidation` `the business is, in the opinion of the liquidator, required for an orderly liquidation`

@export Do the directors' and shareholders' powers pass to the liquidator (s 219(1))?
GIVEN `a court has made an order for liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court made an order for liquidation?
      `the court has specifically authorized the directors or shareholders to keep the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court specifically authorized the directors or shareholders to keep the power?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the directors' and shareholders' powers pass to the liquidator` IF
    `the powers of the directors and shareholders cease and vest in the liquidator within s 219(1)(b)` `a court has made an order for liquidation` `the court has specifically authorized the directors or shareholders to keep the power`

@export May the liquidator hand some of those powers back to the directors or shareholders (s 219(2))?
GIVEN `the power is vested in the liquidator by paragraph 219(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the power one that is vested in the liquidator by paragraph 219(1)(b)?
      `the delegate is the directors or the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the delegate the directors or the shareholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the liquidator hand some of those powers back to the directors or shareholders` IF
    `the liquidator may delegate the power within s 219(2)` `the power is vested in the liquidator by paragraph 219(1)(b)` `the delegate is the directors or the shareholders`

@export Can the court appoint me as liquidator (s 220(1))?
GIVEN `the court is making an order for the liquidation of the corporation, or has made one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court making an order for the liquidation of the corporation, or has it made one?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the court appoint me as liquidator` IF
    `the court may appoint a person as liquidator within s 220(1)` `the court is making an order for the liquidation of the corporation, or has made one`

@export Is the corporation's property under the control of the court while there is no liquidator (s 220(2))?
GIVEN `an order for the liquidation of the corporation has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an order for the liquidation of the corporation been made?
      `the office of liquidator is vacant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the office of liquidator vacant?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation's property under the control of the court while there is no liquidator` IF
    `the property of the corporation is under the control of the court within s 220(2)` `an order for the liquidation of the corporation has been made` `the office of liquidator is vacant`

§§ `The liquidator and the end of a liquidation (Part XVIII, ss 221 to 225)`

-- What the liquidator must and may do, the year within which the final accounts must go to the court,
-- a shareholder's right to a distribution in money, and the duty to keep the records.

@export Must the liquidator give notice of their appointment to the Director and known creditors (s 221(a))?
GIVEN `the liquidator has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the liquidator been appointed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the liquidator give notice of their appointment to the Director and known creditors` IF
    `the liquidator must give notice of the appointment to the Director and each known claimant and creditor within s 221(a)` `the liquidator has been appointed`

@export By what day must a creditor or claimant present particulars of a claim to the liquidator (s 221(b))?
GIVEN `the day the notice was first published` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the liquidator's notice first published? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must a creditor or claimant present particulars of a claim to the liquidator` IS
    `the last day for a person with a claim to present particulars within s 221(b)(iii)` `the day the notice was first published`

@export Did I present particulars of my claim to the liquidator in time (s 221(b))?
GIVEN `the day the notice was first published` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the liquidator's notice first published? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-01)
      `the day the particulars were presented` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you present your particulars in writing to the liquidator? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-09-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I present particulars of my claim to the liquidator in time` IF
    `the particulars were presented in time within s 221(b)(iii)` `the day the notice was first published` `the day the particulars were presented`

@export By what day must the liquidator send the court and the Director the corporation's financial statements (s 221(h))?
GIVEN `the start of the twelve month period` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the twelve month period start (the appointment, or the end of the last period)? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the liquidator send the court and the Director the corporation's financial statements` IS
    `the last day for the financial statements for a twelve month period within s 221(h)` `the start of the twelve month period`

@export Did the liquidator deliver the financial statements in time (s 221(h))?
GIVEN `the start of the twelve month period` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the twelve month period start? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-01)
      `the day the financial statements were delivered to the court` IS A DATE @desc On what day were they delivered to the court? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2027-07-01)
      `the day the financial statements were delivered to the Director` IS A DATE @desc On what day were they delivered to the Director? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2027-07-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the liquidator deliver the financial statements in time` IF
    `the financial statements were delivered in time within s 221(h)` `the start of the twelve month period` `the day the financial statements were delivered to the court` `the day the financial statements were delivered to the Director`

@export Is the form of the liquidator's financial statements acceptable (s 221(h))?
GIVEN `the statements are in the form required by section 155` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the statements in the form required by section 155?
      `the statements are in another form the liquidator thinks proper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they in another form the liquidator thinks proper?
      `the statements are in the form the court requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they in the form the court requires?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the form of the liquidator's financial statements acceptable` IF
    `the form of the financial statements is acceptable within s 221(h)` `the statements are in the form required by section 155` `the statements are in another form the liquidator thinks proper` `the statements are in the form the court requires`

@export Must the liquidator now distribute what is left among the shareholders (s 221(i))?
GIVEN `the court has approved the final accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court approved the final accounts?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the liquidator now distribute what is left among the shareholders` IF
    `the liquidator must distribute the remaining property among the shareholders within s 221(i)` `the court has approved the final accounts`

@export May the liquidator do a given thing for the corporation (s 222(1))?
GIVEN `the act` IS A `Kind of act under s 222(1)` @desc What does the liquidator want to do? Choose the closest listed kind, or "an act the section does not list".
      `the business is required for an orderly liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the act is carrying on the business: is the business required for an orderly liquidation?
      `the thing is necessary for the liquidation of the corporation and the distribution of its property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the act is another thing: is it necessary for the liquidation and the distribution of the corporation's property?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the liquidator do a given thing for the corporation` IS
    `whether a liquidator may do the act within s 222(1)` `the act` `the business is required for an orderly liquidation` `the thing is necessary for the liquidation of the corporation and the distribution of its property`

@export Am I, as liquidator, free of liability for a decision (s 222(2))?
GIVEN `I exercised the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would have exercised in comparable circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you exercise the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would have exercised in comparable circumstances?
      `I relied in good faith on financial statements represented by an officer, or on a written report of the auditor, fairly to reflect the financial condition of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you rely in good faith on financial statements an officer represented, or an auditor's written report, as fairly reflecting the corporation's financial condition?
      `I relied in good faith on a report of a person whose profession lends credibility to a statement made by that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you rely in good faith on a report of a person whose profession lends credibility to a statement made by that person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I, as liquidator, free of liability for a decision` IF
    `the liquidator is not liable within s 222(2)` `I exercised the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would have exercised in comparable circumstances` `I relied in good faith on financial statements represented by an officer, or on a written report of the auditor, fairly to reflect the financial condition of the corporation` `I relied in good faith on a report of a person whose profession lends credibility to a statement made by that person`

@export By what day must the liquidator apply to the court for approval of the final accounts or an extension (s 223(2))?
GIVEN `the day the liquidator was appointed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the liquidator appointed? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the liquidator apply to the court for approval of the final accounts or an extension` IS
    `the last day for the liquidator's application to the court within s 223(2)` `the day the liquidator was appointed`

@export Does the liquidator's application to the court satisfy the Act (s 223(2))?
GIVEN `the day the liquidator was appointed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the liquidator appointed? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-07-01)
      `the day the liquidator applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the liquidator apply to the court? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2027-07-01)
      `the kind of application` IS A `Kind of application under s 223(2)` @desc What was the application for? Choose the closest listed kind.
      `the application sets out the reasons for the extension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was an extension: does the application set out the reasons for it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the liquidator's application to the court satisfy the Act` IF
    `the liquidator's application satisfies s 223(2)` `the day the liquidator was appointed` `the day the liquidator applied` `the kind of application` `the application sets out the reasons for the extension`

@export Can I, as a shareholder, ask the court to make the liquidator show cause (s 223(3))?
GIVEN `I am a shareholder of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shareholder of the corporation?
      `the liquidator has failed to make the application required by subsection 223(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the liquidator failed to make the application that subsection 223(2) requires?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I, as a shareholder, ask the court to make the liquidator show cause` IF
    `a shareholder may apply for an order that the liquidator show cause within s 223(3)` `I am a shareholder of the corporation` `the liquidator has failed to make the application required by subsection 223(2)`

@export Has the liquidator given everyone the notice of intention to apply that the Act requires (s 223(4))?
GIVEN `notice of the intention to apply was given to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice of the intention to apply given to the Director?
      `notice was given to each inspector appointed under section 217` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice given to each inspector appointed under section 217?
      `notice was given to each shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice given to each shareholder?
      `notice was given to each person who provided a security, fidelity bond or fidelity insurance for the liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice given to each person who provided a security, fidelity bond or fidelity insurance for the liquidation?
      `the notice was published in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office, or as otherwise directed by the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice published in a newspaper in the place where the corporation has its registered office, or as the court directed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the liquidator given everyone the notice of intention to apply that the Act requires` IF
    `the liquidator's notice of intention to apply complies with s 223(4)` `notice of the intention to apply was given to the Director` `notice was given to each inspector appointed under section 217` `notice was given to each shareholder` `notice was given to each person who provided a security, fidelity bond or fidelity insurance for the liquidation` `the notice was published in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office, or as otherwise directed by the court`

@export Does the corporation still exist on a given day after the court's final order (s 223(8))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of dissolution` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of dissolution? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2027-09-01)
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know whether it exists? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2027-08-31)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the corporation still exist on a given day after the court's final order` IF
    `the corporation exists on a day within s 223(8)` `the date shown in the certificate of dissolution` `the day asked about`

@export Can I, as a shareholder, ask the court to make the distribution in money (s 224(1))?
GIVEN `the shareholders resolve or the liquidator proposes to exchange all or substantially all the property for securities of another body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the shareholders resolve, or does the liquidator propose, to exchange all or substantially all the corporation's property for securities of another body corporate to be distributed to the shareholders?
      `the shareholders resolve or the liquidator proposes to distribute all or part of the property in kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the shareholders resolve, or does the liquidator propose, to distribute all or part of the corporation's property to the shareholders in kind?
      `the proposal is made in the course of liquidation of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proposal made in the course of liquidation of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I, as a shareholder, ask the court to make the distribution in money` IF
    `a shareholder may apply to the court for a distribution in money within s 224(1)` `the shareholders resolve or the liquidator proposes to exchange all or substantially all the property for securities of another body corporate` `the shareholders resolve or the liquidator proposes to distribute all or part of the property in kind` `the proposal is made in the course of liquidation of the corporation`

@export May the court order the distribution to be in money (s 224(2))?
GIVEN `I have applied under subsection 224(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied to the court under subsection 224(1)?
      `the kind of order` IS A `Kind of order under s 224(2)` @desc What order is being asked for? Choose the closest listed kind, or "an order of another kind than those s 224(2) names".
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court order the distribution to be in money` IF
    `the court may make the order within s 224(2)` `I have applied under subsection 224(1)` `the kind of order`

@export By what day does a custodian of the records stay liable to produce them (s 225(1))?
GIVEN `the end of the prescribed period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the prescribed period end? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2031-12-31)
      `the end of a shorter period fixed by an order made under subsection 223(5)` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc Did a court order under subsection 223(5) fix a shorter period? If so, on what day does it end?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day does a custodian of the records stay liable to produce them` IS
    `the last day the custodian remains liable to produce the documents and records within s 225(1)` `the end of the prescribed period` `the end of a shorter period fixed by an order made under subsection 223(5)`

@export Am I guilty of an offence if I fail to produce records I have custody of (s 225(2))?
GIVEN `I remain liable under subsection 225(1) and have not produced the documents and records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you remain liable under subsection 225(1), and have you not produced the documents and records?
      `I have reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have reasonable cause?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of an offence if I fail to produce records I have custody of` IF
    `the custodian is guilty of an offence within s 225(2)` `I remain liable under subsection 225(1) and have not produced the documents and records` `I have reasonable cause`

@export Is this penalty within what the Act allows for failing to produce records (s 225(2))?
GIVEN `the fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fine, in dollars?
      `the months of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of imprisonment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this penalty within what the Act allows for failing to produce records` IF
    `the penalty is within the limits of s 225(2)` `the fine in dollars` `the months of imprisonment`

§§ `After dissolution (Part XVIII, ss 226 to 228)`

-- A dissolved corporation can still be sued for two years, shareholders who received its property can be
-- made to give it back up to what they got, the share of a missing creditor goes to the Receiver General,
-- and property nobody has dealt with passes to the Crown and comes back on revival.

@export Does "shareholder" in the rules about dissolved corporations include me (s 226(1))?
GIVEN `what I am` IS A `Kind of person for the word shareholder in s 226(1)` @desc What are you in relation to the shares? Choose the closest listed kind, or "a person who is not a shareholder, an heir or a personal representative (s 226(1))".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does "shareholder" in the rules about dissolved corporations include me` IS
    `whether a person is a shareholder within s 226(1)` `what I am`

@export Can a lawsuit begun before the corporation's dissolution go on (s 226(2))?
GIVEN `the body corporate has been dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the body corporate been dissolved?
      `the action or proceeding was commenced by or against the body corporate before its dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the action or proceeding commenced by or against the body corporate before its dissolution?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a lawsuit begun before the corporation's dissolution go on` IF
    `the action may be continued as if the body corporate had not been dissolved within s 226(2)(a)` `the body corporate has been dissolved` `the action or proceeding was commenced by or against the body corporate before its dissolution`

@export By what day can someone still sue a dissolved corporation (s 226(2))?
GIVEN `the date of dissolution` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the body corporate dissolved? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-08-01)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day can someone still sue a dissolved corporation` IS
    `the last day for an action to be brought against the dissolved body corporate within s 226(2)(b)` `the date of dissolution`

@export Can I still sue the dissolved corporation on a given day (s 226(2))?
GIVEN `the date of dissolution` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the body corporate dissolved? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-08-01)
      `the day the action was brought` IS A DATE @desc On what day was or will the action be brought? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2028-08-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I still sue the dissolved corporation on a given day` IF
    `the action may be brought against the dissolved body corporate within s 226(2)(b)` `the date of dissolution` `the day the action was brought`

@export Is the dissolved corporation's property still available to satisfy a judgment (s 226(2))?
GIVEN `the body corporate has been dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the body corporate been dissolved?
      `the property would have been available to satisfy the judgment or order if the body corporate had not been dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the property have been available to satisfy the judgment or order if the body corporate had not been dissolved?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the dissolved corporation's property still available to satisfy a judgment` IF
    `the property remains available to satisfy the judgment or order within s 226(2)(c)` `the body corporate has been dissolved` `the property would have been available to satisfy the judgment or order if the body corporate had not been dissolved`

@export Is service on this person service on a dissolved corporation (s 226(3))?
GIVEN `the person served is shown in the last notice filed under section 106 or 113` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person served shown in the last notice filed under section 106 or 113?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is service on this person service on a dissolved corporation` IS
    `whether service on a dissolved corporation is effected by serving this person within s 226(3)` `the person served is shown in the last notice filed under section 106 or 113`

@export How much can a shareholder who got the corporation's property be made to repay (s 226(4))?
GIVEN `a shareholder received property of the body corporate on a distribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the shareholder receive property of the body corporate on a distribution?
      `the person is claiming under subsection 226(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claimant claiming under subsection 226(2)?
      `the amount the claimant is owed` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the claimant owed?
      `the amount received by the shareholder on the distribution` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did the shareholder receive on the distribution?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much can a shareholder who got the corporation's property be made to repay` IS
    `the most the shareholder is liable to pay within s 226(4)` `a shareholder received property of the body corporate on a distribution` `the person is claiming under subsection 226(2)` `the amount the claimant is owed` `the amount received by the shareholder on the distribution`

@export Is a claim against a former shareholder brought in time (s 226(4))?
GIVEN `the date of dissolution` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the body corporate dissolved? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-08-01)
      `the day the action was brought` IS A DATE @desc On what day was or will the action be brought? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2028-08-01)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a claim against a former shareholder brought in time` IF
    `the action against a shareholder is brought in time within s 226(4)` `the date of dissolution` `the day the action was brought`

@export May a referee require a given contribution from me as a former shareholder (s 226(5))?
GIVEN `the plaintiff has established a claim in an action brought against the former shareholders as a class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the plaintiff established a claim in an action brought against the former shareholders as a class?
      `the amount I received on the distribution` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you receive on the distribution?
      `the amount the referee proposes I contribute` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does the referee propose you contribute?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a referee require a given contribution from me as a former shareholder` IF
    `the referee may require this contribution within s 226(5)(b)` `the plaintiff has established a claim in an action brought against the former shareholders as a class` `the amount I received on the distribution` `the amount the referee proposes I contribute`

@export Must my share go to the Receiver General if I cannot be found (s 227(1))?
GIVEN `the body corporate has been dissolved under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the body corporate been dissolved under the Act?
      `I, as a creditor or shareholder, cannot be found` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the creditor or shareholder one who cannot be found?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my share go to the Receiver General if I cannot be found` IF
    `the portion must be converted into money and paid to the Receiver General within s 227(1)` `the body corporate has been dissolved under this Act` `I, as a creditor or shareholder, cannot be found`

@export How much will the Receiver General pay me if I prove my entitlement (s 227(3))?
GIVEN `the moneys paid to the Receiver General to which the person is entitled` IS A NUMBER @desc How much money paid to the Receiver General are you entitled to?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will the Receiver General pay me if I prove my entitlement` IS
    `the amount the Receiver General pays within s 227(3)` `the moneys paid to the Receiver General to which the person is entitled`

@export Does the corporation's leftover property pass to the Crown on dissolution (s 228(1))?
GIVEN `the body corporate has been dissolved under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the body corporate been dissolved under the Act?
      `the property had not been disposed of at the date of dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the property not been disposed of at the date of dissolution?
      `the property remains available under subsection 226(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the property remain available under subsection 226(2)?
      `the property is the portion within section 227` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property the portion of a creditor's or shareholder's share that falls within section 227?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the corporation's leftover property pass to the Crown on dissolution` IF
    `the property vests in Her Majesty in right of Canada within s 228(1)` `the body corporate has been dissolved under this Act` `the property had not been disposed of at the date of dissolution` `the property remains available under subsection 226(2)` `the property is the portion within section 227`

@export Does the revived corporation get its property back (s 228(2))?
GIVEN `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the body corporate been revived as a corporation under section 209?
      `the property is not money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property something other than money?
      `the property vested in Her Majesty under subsection 228(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the property vest in Her Majesty under subsection 228(1)?
      `the property has not been disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the property not been disposed of?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the revived corporation get its property back` IF
    `the property is returned to the corporation within s 228(2)` `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209` `the property is not money` `the property vested in Her Majesty under subsection 228(1)` `the property has not been disposed of`

@export How much money does the revived corporation get back for money the Crown received (s 228(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the body corporate been revived as a corporation under section 209?
      `the money received by Her Majesty under subsection 228(1)` IS A NUMBER @desc How much money did Her Majesty receive under subsection 228(1)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much money does the revived corporation get back for money the Crown received` IS
    `the amount paid to the corporation under s 228(2)(a)` `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209` `the money received by Her Majesty under subsection 228(1)`

@export How much does the revived corporation get back for property the Crown has sold (s 228(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the body corporate been revived as a corporation under section 209?
      `property other than money vested in Her Majesty under subsection 228(1) and has been disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did property other than money vest in Her Majesty under subsection 228(1), and has it been disposed of?
      `the value of the property at the date it vested` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the value of the property at the date it vested?
      `the amount realized by Her Majesty from the disposition` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount did Her Majesty realize from the disposition?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much does the revived corporation get back for property the Crown has sold` IS
    `the amount paid to the corporation under s 228(2)(b)` `the body corporate is revived as a corporation under section 209` `property other than money vested in Her Majesty under subsection 228(1) and has been disposed of` `the value of the property at the date it vested` `the amount realized by Her Majesty from the disposition`
